('adobe', 'Adobe', 'productivity', 'Connect AI assistants to Adobe''s creative tools (Photoshop, Lightroom, Illustrator, Firefly, Premiere, Express, InDesign, Stock) through Adobe''s hosted MCP server.', '/services/adobe.png?tone=light', '{"name":"Adobe","slug":"adobe","inputs":[],"skills":[{"body":"# Adobe for creativity\n\nOn first connection your MCP client opens a browser window to sign in with your Adobe ID and authorize access; credentials are reused for later sessions.\n\nOnce connected, the server exposes tools that connect Photoshop, Lightroom, Illustrator, Firefly, Premiere, Express, InDesign, and Stock capabilities to AI-assisted creative work. Discover the available tools after authenticating and invoke them to generate and edit creative assets.","name":"adobe-usage","description":"How to use the Adobe for creativity MCP tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Connect AI assistants to Adobe''s creative tools (Photoshop, Lightroom, Illustrator, Firefly, Premiere, Express, InDesign, Stock) through Adobe''s hosted MCP server.","category":"productivity","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://adobe-creativity.adobe.io/mcp","args":[],"name":"adobe","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"description":"The Adobe for creativity remote MCP server is a hosted Model Context Protocol endpoint that lets AI clients drive Adobe''s creative applications and services. It authenticates through a browser-based Adobe ID sign-in, so no API key needs to be stored. Tools cover creative generation and editing across Photoshop, Lightroom, Illustrator, Firefly, Premiere, Express, InDesign, and Stock."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[0.011154175,0.006793976,0.034576416,0.015670776,0.0058670044,-0.051635742,0.020889282,0.07312012,-0.014625549,0.018035889,0.02017212,-0.006450653,0.005718231,-0.014411926,-0.014213562,0.0146102905,-0.03942871,-0.024856567,-0.0058250427,0.01939392,0.0072746277,0.05810547,0.008621216,0.043060303,-0.0013084412,-0.008285522,-0.07232666,-0.018157959,0.031707764,-0