('attio', 'Attio', 'crm', 'Search, create and update Attio CRM records, lists, notes and tasks from your agent.', '/services/attio.png?tone=light', '{"name":"Attio","slug":"attio","inputs":[],"skills":[{"body":"# Attio\n\nThe Attio MCP server exposes your Attio CRM workspace: people, companies, deals, custom objects, lists, notes, tasks, comments, emails, meetings and call recordings.\n\n## Auth\n\nConnecting opens an Attio sign-in in the browser. No API key. The agent acts with your own Attio permissions.\n\n## How to work\n\n- Start with `whoami` and `list-objects` to learn the workspace; call `list-attribute-definitions` before writing so you use real attribute slugs.\n- Find records with `search-records` (full text) or `list-records` (filters, sorting), then `get-records-by-ids` for details.\n- Prefer `upsert-record` over `create-record` when a matching attribute exists (email, domain) to avoid duplicates; use `merge-records` to clean existing ones.\n- Pipelines live in lists: `list-lists`, `list-records-in-list`, `add-record-to-list`, `update-list-entry-by-id`.\n- Log context with `create-note`, `create-task` and `create-comment`; find past context with `semantic-search-notes`, `semantic-search-emails`, `search-meetings` and `get-call-recording`.\n- Use `run-basic-report` for totals and breakdowns.\n\n## Limits\n\nWrite tools ask for confirmation. Search tools share 300 requests/minute and semantic search is capped at 2 requests/second: batch lookups instead of looping.","name":"attio-usage","description":"How to use the Attio CRM MCP tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Search, create and update Attio CRM records, lists, notes and tasks from your agent.","category":"crm","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.attio.com/mcp","args":[],"name":"attio","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"description":"Attio is a flexible CRM for people, companies, deals and custom objects. Its hosted MCP server gives the agent read and write access to records, lists, not