('audible', 'Audible', 'productivity', 'Get personalized audiobook and podcast recommendations and previews from Audible using natural-language preferences.', '/services/audible.svg', '{"name":"Audible","slug":"audible","inputs":[],"skills":[{"body":"# Audible\n\nAudible''s remote MCP server provides audiobook and podcast discovery.\n\n## Connecting\n\n- Endpoint: `https://mcp.audible.com/mcp` (HTTP transport).\n- Auth: browser OAuth. On first use your MCP client opens a window to sign in / authorize; credentials are reused afterwards. No API key to paste.\n\n## What it does\n\n- Recommends titles by genre, mood, topic, author, or free-form natural-language preferences.\n- Returns previews and catalog context, scoped to the user''s Audible marketplace/region.\n\n## Tips\n\n- Ask in natural language, e.g. \"suggest a 6-hour sci-fi audiobook with a strong narrator\" or \"podcasts like <show>\".\n- Availability and titles can differ by region.","name":"audible-usage","description":"How to use the Audible MCP tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Get personalized audiobook and podcast recommendations and previews from Audible using natural-language preferences.","category":"productivity","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.audible.com/mcp","args":[],"name":"audible","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"description":"Audible''s official hosted MCP server lets AI assistants surface audiobook and podcast recommendations by genre, mood, topic, or other natural-language preferences, scoped to the user''s marketplace region. It connects over a remote HTTP endpoint and authenticates through a browser OAuth sign-in, so no API key or credential ever needs to be pasted."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.0009551048,-0.0102005005,0.005870819,0.024459839,-0.033966064,-0.019744873,0.03225708,0.055633545,0.035369873,0.0021152496,0.016662598,-0.013519287,-0.039489746,0.011558533,0.00017511845,0.0309906,-0.022338867,-0.040771484,-0.0077667236,0.03189087,0.0015859604,0.056762695,0.