('beehiiv', 'beehiiv', 'marketing', 'Analyse your beehiiv newsletter: posts, subscribers, growth and revenue metrics.', '/services/beehiiv.png?tone=light', '{"name":"beehiiv","slug":"beehiiv","inputs":[],"skills":[{"body":"# beehiiv\n\nUse the beehiiv tools to read a newsletter publication: posts and their performance, subscribers and segments, growth and revenue analytics, podcasts, automations, products, surveys, polls and referrals.\n\n- Start by listing publications and pick the right one; most tools are scoped to a publication.\n- For performance questions, pull post-level stats (opens, clicks, unsubscribes) rather than guessing from titles.\n- For growth questions, combine subscriber counts over time with acquisition source and referral data.\n- This connection is read-only: never claim a post was published, edited or scheduled. If asked to write or send, report the data you gathered and state that the action must be done in beehiiv.","name":"beehiiv-usage","description":"How to use beehiiv tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Analyse your beehiiv newsletter: posts, subscribers, growth and revenue metrics.","category":"marketing","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.beehiiv.com/mcp","args":[],"name":"beehiiv","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"description":"Connects beehiiv''s hosted MCP server. You sign in with your beehiiv account; no API key to paste. The current MCP version is read-only: it can read posts, subscribers, analytics, podcasts, automations, products, surveys, polls and referrals, but cannot publish or edit."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.0020332336,0.009399414,0.0524292,-0.016540527,0.0017089844,-0.04345703,-0.022949219,0.04046631,0.025756836,0.0065460205,0.03894043,-0.009979248,-0.02128601,0.012321472,-0.0037441254,0.028900146,0.001750946,-0.021881104,-0.022567749,0.055389404,0.038726807,0.029769897,0.068359375,0.044036865,0.005996704,-0.0067443848,-0.097229004,-0.015625,0.021224976,-0.04260254,0.04257202,-0.022125244,-0.005844116,0