('bitly', 'Bitly', 'marketing', 'Create, customize, and track short links and QR codes through Bitly''s hosted MCP server.', '/services/bitly.svg', '{"name":"Bitly","slug":"bitly","skills":[{"body":"# Bitly\n\nBitly''s MCP server lets you manage short links and QR codes and read their analytics.\n\n## Common tasks\n- Shorten a long URL into a Bitly link, optionally with a custom back-half.\n- Create and customize branded short links.\n- Generate QR codes for a destination or existing link.\n- Retrieve click and scan analytics (over time, by country, by referrer).\n\n## Tips\n- Reference an existing link by its Bitlink id (e.g. `bit.ly/abc123`) when fetching analytics.\n- Ask for a specific date range when pulling click metrics.\n","name":"bitly-usage","description":"How to use Bitly MCP tools"}],"summary":"Create, customize, and track short links and QR codes through Bitly''s hosted MCP server.","category":"marketing","authMethods":[{"id":"oauth","kind":"oauth","label":"Sign in with Bitly","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://api-ssl.bitly.com/v4/mcp","args":[],"name":"bitly","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":true},{"id":"api-token","kind":"key","label":"Access token","inputs":[{"key":"BITLY_ACCESS_TOKEN","help":"In Bitly: log in at bitly.com -> Settings -> API -> Generate Access Token. Copy and store it; it is sent as a Bearer token.","type":"password","label":"Bitly access token","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"your Bitly access token"}],"envKeys":[],"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://api-ssl.bitly.com/v4/mcp","args":[],"name":"bitly","headers":{"Authorization":"Bearer ${input.BITLY_ACCESS_TOKEN}"},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":false}],"description":"Bitly is a link management platform for shortening, branding, and analyzing links and QR codes. Its hosted MCP server exposes tools to create and customize links, generate QR codes, and read click and scan analytics. Connect via browser OAuth (r