('browser-use', 'Browser Use', 'seo', 'Run cloud browser agents that navigate sites, fill forms and extract structured data.', '/services/browser-use.png?tone=light', '{"name":"Browser Use","slug":"browser-use","inputs":[{"key":"BROWSER_USE_API_KEY","help":"Find it in Browser Use → Settings → API Keys (cloud.browser-use.com/settings?tab=api-keys).","type":"password","label":"Browser Use API key","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"bu_…"}],"skills":[{"body":"# Browser Use\n\nRun web tasks in a real cloud browser. Start with run_session, giving `task` a precise, step-by-step instruction (which site, what to click, what to bring back) and an `output_schema` whenever you need structured data rather than prose.\n\nrun_session returns immediately: poll get_session until the status is done or failed, then read the result. get_session_messages shows the agent''s actions and reasoning when a run goes wrong. Set `keep_alive: true` to reuse the same browser for follow-ups via send_task, and always stop_session when you are finished, since idle browser time is billed.\n\nFor a site that requires a login, call list_browser_profiles first and pass the matching `profile_id`. list_sessions recaps recent runs with their status and cost.\n\nBrowser sessions are slow and metered: prefer a plain HTTP fetch or a scraping tool for static public pages, and reach for Browser Use when the task needs real interaction (login, clicks, multi-step flows, JS-heavy apps).","name":"browser-use-usage","description":"How to use Browser Use tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Run cloud browser agents that navigate sites, fill forms and extract structured data.","category":"seo","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://api.browser-use.com/v3/mcp","args":[],"name":"browser-use","headers":{"x-browser-use-api-key":"${input.BROWSER_USE_API_KEY}"},"transport":"http"}],"description":"Connects Browser Use''s hosted MCP server so the agent can drive a real cloud browser: navigate, click, fill forms, log in