('calendly', 'Calendly', 'productivity', 'Connect AI assistants to Calendly to check availability, look up scheduled events, and manage booking links.', '/services/calendly.svg', '{"name":"Calendly","slug":"calendly","inputs":[],"skills":[{"body":"# Calendly\n\nThe Calendly MCP server connects to your Calendly account over streamable HTTP. On first use, your MCP client opens a browser window to sign in and authorize access (OAuth 2.1 with PKCE); credentials are then reused for future sessions.\n\n## What you can do\n\n- Check availability across your Calendly event types\n- Look up scheduled events and invitee details\n- Manage and share booking links using your existing Calendly setup\n\n## Notes\n\n- No API key or personal access token is required or supported; authentication is browser OAuth only.\n- Scopes cover scheduling read and write access.","name":"calendly-usage","description":"How to use the Calendly MCP tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Connect AI assistants to Calendly to check availability, look up scheduled events, and manage booking links.","category":"productivity","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.calendly.com","args":[],"name":"calendly","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"description":"Calendly''s official hosted MCP server lets assistants read your availability, look up scheduled events, and manage booking links using your existing Calendly setup. It connects over streamable HTTP and authenticates through a browser OAuth sign-in, so no API key or token needs to be pasted.","multiInstance":true}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.00075912476,-0.0008172989,0.035247803,-0.005908966,-0.035980225,-0.040283203,0.0151901245,0.013893127,0.025131226,0.021072388,0.02822876,-0.020385742,0.014266968,0.0035991669,0.004928589,0.032287598,-0.06323242,0.0025558472,-0.029541016,0.051361084,-0.010658264,0.06964111,0.009338379,0.024353027,-0.0016736984,-0.0039482117,-0.0546875,0.03463745,0.005584717,0.0038604736,0.024383545,-0.030883789,-0.033203125,0.0