('clay', 'Clay', 'crm', 'Enrich leads and companies by pushing records to a Clay table.', '/services/clay.png', '{"name":"Clay","slug":"clay","inputs":[{"key":"CLAY_WEBHOOK_URL","help":"In your Clay table, add a ''Webhook'' source (Pull records into Clay) and copy its URL.","type":"url","label":"Clay table webhook URL","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"https://api.clay.com/v3/sources/webhook/…"},{"key":"CLAY_API_KEY","help":"Find it in Clay → Settings → Account → API key (used for Clay-native table lookups).","type":"password","label":"Clay API key","secret":true,"required":false,"placeholder":"Your Clay API key"}],"skills":[{"body":"# Clay\n\nClay enriches leads and companies. There is no hosted MCP server — drive Clay over HTTP using the values in the engine environment.\n\n## Push records for enrichment\nPOST a JSON record to the table webhook URL in `CLAY_WEBHOOK_URL`:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \"$CLAY_WEBHOOK_URL\" \\\n  -H ''Content-Type: application/json'' \\\n  -d ''{\"email\":\"jane@acme.com\",\"company\":\"Acme\",\"linkedin\":\"https://linkedin.com/in/jane\"}''\n```\n\nEach POST adds one row to that Clay table and runs its enrichment columns. Send only the fields the table expects, and confirm the records with the user before sending.\n\n## Lookups\nIf `CLAY_API_KEY` is set, use it for Clay-native table lookups. Never reveal the API key or the webhook URL in chat.","name":"clay-usage","description":"How to enrich records with Clay"}],"envKeys":[{"key":"CLAY_WEBHOOK_URL","fromInput":"CLAY_WEBHOOK_URL"},{"key":"CLAY_API_KEY","fromInput":"CLAY_API_KEY"}],"summary":"Enrich leads and companies by pushing records to a Clay table.","category":"crm","mcpServers":[],"description":"Clay is a GTM data-enrichment platform. It has no official hosted MCP, so the agent drives it over HTTP: it POSTs records to your Clay table''s webhook URL to trigger that table''s enrichment (emails, firmographics, signals). An optional API key enables Clay-native table lookups