('clerk', 'Clerk', 'dev', 'Clerk''s official hosted MCP server gives AI coding assistants up-to-date Clerk SDK snippets and implementation patterns.', '/services/clerk.svg', '{"name":"Clerk","slug":"clerk","inputs":[],"skills":[{"body":"# Clerk MCP\n\nClerk''s hosted MCP server provides up-to-date Clerk SDK code snippets and implementation patterns for AI coding assistants.\n\n## Tools\n\n- `list_clerk_sdk_snippets` — list all available snippets and bundles (frameworks, features, patterns).\n- `clerk_sdk_snippet` — fetch SDK code snippets and patterns for a specific feature or framework.\n\n## Typical flow\n\n1. Call `list_clerk_sdk_snippets` to discover what snippets exist for the target framework (Next.js, Express, React, etc.).\n2. Call `clerk_sdk_snippet` for the specific feature you are implementing (sign-in, route protection, B2B organizations, middleware).\n3. Use the returned code as the current, canonical reference when writing Clerk integration code.\n\nUse this whenever adding or updating Clerk authentication so the generated code matches Clerk''s latest SDK.\n","name":"clerk-usage","description":"How to use the Clerk MCP tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Clerk''s official hosted MCP server gives AI coding assistants up-to-date Clerk SDK snippets and implementation patterns.","category":"dev","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.clerk.com/mcp","args":[],"name":"clerk","headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"description":"Clerk is an authentication and user-management platform for web and mobile apps. Its official remote MCP server exposes tools that return current Clerk SDK code snippets, route-protection patterns, and framework-specific guidance so AI agents can write correct Clerk integrations. The public documentation endpoint needs no credentials to connect."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.0154800415,0.025512695,0.015563965,-0.00018835068,0.01096344,0.038879395,0.018630981,0.038391113,0.00793457,0.02708435,0.044952393,-0.046295166,0.015266418,0.008087158