('cockroachdb', 'CockroachDB Cloud', 'dev', 'Connect AI agents to your CockroachDB Cloud clusters to inspect schemas, check cluster health, and run read-only SQL through the managed MCP server.', '/services/cockroachdb.svg', '{"name":"CockroachDB Cloud","slug":"cockroachdb","skills":[{"body":"# CockroachDB Cloud MCP\n\nThe managed MCP server connects to a single CockroachDB Cloud cluster (selected by the `mcp-cluster-id` header). You can authenticate either by signing in through your browser via OAuth 2.1, or with a CockroachDB Cloud service account API key.\n\n## What you can do\n- List databases and tables\n- Describe table schemas and indexes\n- Inspect cluster health and currently running queries\n- Run read-only SQL and `EXPLAIN` statements to analyze query plans\n\n## Notes\n- The server is read-only by default; write operations require explicit opt-in consent.\n- All access is scoped to the cluster ID you provide.\n","name":"cockroachdb-usage","description":"How to use the CockroachDB Cloud MCP tools"}],"summary":"Connect AI agents to your CockroachDB Cloud clusters to inspect schemas, check cluster health, and run read-only SQL through the managed MCP server.","category":"dev","authMethods":[{"id":"oauth","kind":"oauth","label":"Sign in with OAuth","inputs":[{"key":"CLUSTER_ID","help":"Find it in the CockroachDB Cloud Console: open your cluster and copy the ID (a UUID) from the page URL (cockroachlabs.cloud/cluster/<id>) or from the Connect modal''s MCP snippet.","type":"text","label":"CockroachDB Cloud cluster ID","secret":false,"required":true,"placeholder":"xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx"}],"envKeys":[],"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://cockroachlabs.cloud/mcp","args":[],"name":"cockroachdb-cloud","oauth":{},"headers":{"mcp-cluster-id":"${input.CLUSTER_ID}"},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":true},{"id":"api-key","kind":"key","label":"Service account API key","inputs":[{"key":"CLUSTER_ID","help":"Find it in the CockroachDB Cloud Console: open your cluster and copy the ID (a UUID) from the page URL (cockroachlabs.cloud/cluster/<id>) or from the Connect modal''s MCP snippet.","type":"text","label":"CockroachDB Cloud cluster ID","secret":false,"required":true,"placeholder":"xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx"},{"key":"API_KEY","help":"Create a service account and its API key in the CockroachDB Cloud Console (Organization > Access Management > Service Accounts), granting it a role scoped to the target cluster.","type":"password","label":"CockroachDB Cloud API key","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"your CockroachDB Cloud API key"}],"envKeys":[],"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://cockroachlabs.cloud/mcp","args":[],"name":"cockroachdb-cloud","headers":{"Authorization":"Bearer ${input.API_KEY}","mcp-cluster-id":"${input.CLUSTER_ID}"},"transport":"http"}]}],"description":"CockroachDB Cloud exposes an official managed MCP server that lets AI tools list databases and tables, describe schemas and indexes, inspect cluster health and running queries, and run read-only SQL and EXPLAIN statements. It is read-only by default with writes gated behind explicit consent. Authenticate via browser-based OAuth 2.1 or a service account API key, scoped to a specific cluster."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[0.011299133,0.027801514,0.053100586,0.0070152283,0.019363403,-0.017868042,-0.013801575,0.043182373,-0.029922485,-0.009292603,0.035308838,-0.02999878,0.028625488,0.025466919,-0.031082153,0.010719299,-0.052520752,0.0051345825,0.003572464,0.06378174,-0.0070533752,0.017120361,0.030044556,0.0047569275,-0.054138184,0.04046631,-0.04638672,-0.002166748,0.018630981,-0.029632568,0.006942749,-0.030792236,-0.04373169,0.011054993,0.027572632,-0.012252808,-0.0023918152,0.04989624,0.009971619,0.011886597,-0.025054932,-0.0046577454,0.020751953,0.023040771,-0.0016345978,-0.0070762634,-0.0017757416,-0.029632568,0.006839752,-0.0020771027,-0.061950684,0.04144287,-0.016204834,0.015258789,-0.012168884,0.020401001,0.016235352,0.029586792,0