('context7', 'Context7', 'dev', 'Fetch up-to-date, version-specific documentation and code examples for any library directly into the agent''s context.', '/services/context7.png', '{"name":"Context7","slug":"context7","skills":[{"body":"# Context7\n\nUse the context7_* tools to fetch current, version-specific documentation and code examples for software libraries and frameworks.\n\n## Typical flow\n1. Call the resolve/library-id tool with the library name (e.g. \"next.js\", \"supabase\") to get the Context7-compatible library ID.\n2. Call the get-docs tool with that library ID to retrieve up-to-date documentation. Optionally scope by a topic (e.g. \"routing\", \"authentication\") to narrow the results.\n\n## When to use\n- Before writing code against an external library, especially for recent or version-specific APIs, to avoid outdated or hallucinated usage.\n- When the user references a specific framework version and you need accurate, current examples.\n\nAuthentication uses either browser-based OAuth sign-in or your Context7 API key (header CONTEXT7_API_KEY). It works without a key at lower rate limits, but signing in or providing a key is recommended for higher limits.","name":"context7-usage","description":"Pull up-to-date library documentation and code examples into context via Context7."}],"summary":"Fetch up-to-date, version-specific documentation and code examples for any library directly into the agent''s context.","category":"dev","authMethods":[{"id":"oauth","kind":"oauth","label":"Sign in with OAuth","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.context7.com/mcp/oauth","args":[],"name":"context7","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":true},{"id":"api-key","kind":"key","label":"API key","inputs":[{"key":"API_KEY","help":"Generate a free API key at context7.com/dashboard (Dashboard > API Keys). Recommended for higher rate limits.","type":"password","label":"Context7 API Key","secret":true,"required":true,"placeho