('dbt', 'dbt', 'analytics', 'Query and explore your governed dbt data assets, metrics, and models through the official remote dbt MCP server.', '/services/dbt.png', '{"name":"dbt","slug":"dbt","inputs":[{"key":"DBT_TOKEN","help":"Create a Personal Access Token (or a service token with Semantic Layer + Developer permissions) in the dbt platform under Account settings -> API tokens / Personal tokens. execute_sql requires a PAT rather than a service token.","type":"password","label":"dbt access token","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"dbtc_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"},{"key":"DBT_PROD_ENVIRONMENT_ID","help":"The numeric ID of your production dbt environment. Find it in the dbt platform under Orchestration (open your production environment; the ID is the number in the environment''s URL). Enter digits only, no URL.","type":"text","label":"Production environment ID","secret":false,"required":true,"placeholder":"54321"}],"skills":[{"body":"# dbt (remote MCP)\n\nThis connector talks to dbt Labs'' official remote MCP server, hosted on the dbt platform. It exposes read/metadata tools over your governed dbt project.\n\n## Endpoint & auth\n- URL: `https://cloud.getdbt.com/api/ai/v1/mcp/` by default. If your account is on a region host (e.g. `emea.dbt.com`, `au.dbt.com`) or a multi-cell account (`ACCOUNT_PREFIX.us1.dbt.com`), replace the url with the MCP Endpoint URL shown under **Account settings -> Access URLs**.\n- Auth is header-based: `Authorization: Token <access token>` plus `x-dbt-prod-environment-id: <numeric prod environment id>`.\n\n## Common tools\n- **Discovery / metadata**: list models, sources, and exposures; inspect model details, columns, and lineage.\n- **Semantic Layer**: list metrics and dimensions and query governed metrics so numbers stay consistent with the semantic definitions.\n- **text_to_sql**: turn a natural-language question into SQL against the modeled data (consumes dbt Copilot action allotment).\n- **execute_sql**: run SQL against the warehouse. This requires a PAT (not a service token) and additional `x-dbt-dev-environment-id` and `x-dbt-user-id` headers, which are not configured here by default.\n\n## Tips\n- Available tools depend on your dbt plan, because they rely on APIs (Discovery API, Semantic Layer API) that vary by plan.\n- Prefer Semantic Layer metric queries over raw SQL when a metric already exists, so results respect governance.\n","name":"dbt-usage","description":"How to use the remote dbt MCP tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Query and explore your governed dbt data assets, metrics, and models through the official remote dbt MCP server.","category":"analytics","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://cloud.getdbt.com/api/ai/v1/mcp/","args":[],"name":"dbt","headers":{"Authorization":"Token ${input.DBT_TOKEN}","x-dbt-prod-environment-id":"${input.DBT_PROD_ENVIRONMENT_ID}"},"transport":"http"}],"description":"dbt (data build tool) is the platform teams use to transform, test, and govern data in their warehouse. This connector uses dbt Labs'' official remote MCP server to let an agent discover models, look up column-level lineage and metadata via the Discovery API, query governed metrics through the Semantic Layer, and run text-to-SQL against your production dbt environment."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.019638062,0.01386261,0.095581055,0.009666443,-0.05810547,0.00026750565,-0.0003042221,0.053619385,-0.03945923,0.008003235,0.025802612,-0.0042304993,0.03640747,-0.02357483,0.023239136,0.053100586,-0.0078048706,0.0048446655,-0.027328491,0.05456543,0.035095215,0.048461914,0.03289795,-0.012207031,0.012611389,0.008171082,-0.035186768,0.013412476,0.010063171,-0.016235352,-0.019714355,-0.01979065,-0.029846191,-0.036621094,0.06274414,0.040252686,-0.0129776,0.038848877,0.017990112,0.012886047,-0.059051514,-0.026550293,-0.009414673,0.056396484,-0.028396606,-0.037231445,-0.04083252,-0.018447876,0.03778076,-0.009002686,0.00010448694,0.027404785,-0.018539429,0.047698975,-0.009521484,-0.00039577484,-0.0011262894,