('deepgram', 'Deepgram', 'dev', 'Give agents access to Deepgram''s speech-to-text, text-to-speech, and audio intelligence APIs.', '/services/deepgram.svg', '{"name":"Deepgram","slug":"deepgram","inputs":[{"key":"DEEPGRAM_API_KEY","help":"Create one in the Deepgram Console at console.deepgram.com: select your project, open API Keys in the sidebar, and click Create Key. The key is shown only once, so copy it immediately.","type":"password","label":"Deepgram API key","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"your Deepgram API key"}],"skills":[{"body":"# Deepgram\n\nDeepgram provides voice AI: speech-to-text, text-to-speech, and audio intelligence.\n\n## Tools\n- `transcribe_audio` — transcribe an audio file or URL to text.\n- `synthesize_speech` — generate speech audio from text.\n- `analyze_text` — run audio/text intelligence analysis (summaries, topics, sentiment).\n- `list_models` — list available Deepgram models.\n- `get_usage` — check project usage.\n\n## Auth\nAuthentication uses your `DEEPGRAM_API_KEY`, created in the Deepgram Console (console.deepgram.com → API Keys → Create Key). The server runs locally over stdio via `uvx deepgram-mcp` and reads the key from the environment.\n\n## Tips\n- Provide audio as a public URL or local file path depending on the tool''s supported input.\n- Use `list_models` first if you are unsure which transcription or TTS model to request.","name":"deepgram-usage","description":"How to use the Deepgram MCP tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Give agents access to Deepgram''s speech-to-text, text-to-speech, and audio intelligence APIs.","category":"dev","mcpServers":[{"env":{"DEEPGRAM_API_KEY":"${input.DEEPGRAM_API_KEY}"},"args":["deepgram-mcp"],"name":"deepgram","command":"uvx","headers":{},"transport":"stdio"}],"description":"Deepgram is a voice AI platform offering high-accuracy speech-to-text transcription, text-to-speech synthesis, and audio understanding. Its official MCP server exposes tools to transcribe audio, synthesize spe