('discord', 'Discord', 'productivity', 'Send messages, manage channels, roles and members across your Discord servers.', '/services/discord.svg', '{"name":"Discord","slug":"discord","inputs":[{"key":"DISCORD_TOKEN","help":"Create a bot at discord.com/developers/applications → Bot → Copy Token. Enable Message Content, Server Members and Presence intents, then invite the bot to your server.","type":"password","label":"Discord bot token","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"MTk4N…"}],"skills":[{"body":"# Discord\n\nThe tools are exposed with the server name in front, so they are called discord_discord_login, discord_discord_read_messages and so on. Call mcp_status if you need the exact list.\n\n- Start by calling discord_discord_login, then discord_discord_list_servers and discord_discord_get_server_info to resolve the server and channel IDs you need before acting.\n- discord_discord_read_messages returns at most 100 messages per call. To cover a longer window, page backwards: set `before` to the oldest message you already have and repeat until you reach your starting point.\n- `before`, `after` and `around` accept a snowflake ID or an ISO 8601 date, so `after: \"2026-08-10T08:01:00Z\"` lands straight on a watermark instead of guessing.\n- Never advance a watermark past a window you have not actually read.\n- Send messages with discord_discord_send; edit, delete or search with the message tools; add reactions where useful.\n- Manage channels, categories, forum posts, roles, members and webhooks with the corresponding tools.\n- Always confirm the target server and channel before posting, and never echo the bot token.","name":"discord-usage","description":"How to use Discord tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Send messages, manage channels, roles and members across your Discord servers.","category":"productivity","mcpServers":[{"env":{"DISCORD_TOKEN":"${input.DISCORD_TOKEN}"},"args":["-y","github:Lumvika-build/mcp-discord#v1.4.1-lumvika.1","--config","${input.DISCO