('doordash', 'DoorDash', 'ecommerce', 'Search restaurants, browse menus, and plan food-delivery orders through DoorDash''s official remote MCP server.', '/services/doordash.svg', '{"name":"DoorDash","slug":"doordash","inputs":[],"skills":[{"body":"# DoorDash\n\nThe DoorDash MCP server connects to the official hosted endpoint at `https://openapi.doordash.com/mcp/consumer` over Streamable HTTP.\n\n## Authentication\n\nAuthentication uses browser-based OAuth. The first time you connect, your MCP client opens a browser window to sign in to DoorDash and authorize access; credentials are then reused for future sessions. There is no API key to paste.\n\n## Usage\n\nUse the tools to search for restaurants, browse menus, compare food options, and plan orders. Ask the assistant naturally, for example: \"Find sushi restaurants near me and compare their menu prices.\"\n","name":"doordash-usage","description":"How to use DoorDash MCP tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Search restaurants, browse menus, and plan food-delivery orders through DoorDash''s official remote MCP server.","category":"ecommerce","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://openapi.doordash.com/mcp/consumer","args":[],"name":"doordash","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"description":"DoorDash provides an official hosted Model Context Protocol server that lets AI assistants explore restaurants, compare menus and prices, and work with local dining context. It connects over Streamable HTTP and authenticates with browser-based OAuth, so no API key is required."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[0.0048103333,-0.024093628,0.0137786865,-0.0024604797,0.006652832,-0.011871338,0.0064468384,0.08843994,-0.0021533966,0.0031490326,-0.0046958923,-0.02520752,0.020828247,-0.028793335,-0.00043964386,0.039733887,-0.017700195,-0.019073486,-0.02168274,0.07397461,0.037200928,0.037109375,0.021743774,-0.0070991516,-0.0029754639,0.009025574,-0.04650879,0.008468628,0.006385803,-0.022201538,0.0259552,-0.008598328,-0.039398193,-0.02217102,0