('dublab', 'DubLab', 'marketing', 'Dub videos into 90+ languages with AI voice cloning that keeps the original voice.', '/services/dublab.png', '{"name":"DubLab","slug":"dublab","inputs":[{"key":"DUBLAB_API_KEY","help":"Create it in DubLab -> Account Settings -> API Keys -> Create new key (copy it, it is shown once). API access requires the Pro plan.","type":"password","label":"DubLab API key","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"Your DubLab API key"}],"skills":[{"body":"# DubLab\n\nDubLab dubs videos into 90+ languages with voice cloning. There is no MCP server;\ncall its REST API with curl.\n\n- Base URL: `https://dublab.app/api/v2`\n- Auth header: `apikey: $DUBLAB_API_KEY` (`Authorization: Bearer` is also accepted)\n- The key is available in the environment as `DUBLAB_API_KEY`. Never print it.\n- Fields are snake_case. Errors return `{\"error\":\"message\"}` with 400/401/402/404/413/502/500.\n\n## 1. Check credits and languages\n```bash\ncurl -sS https://dublab.app/api/v2/me -H \"apikey: $DUBLAB_API_KEY\"\n```\n`seconds` is the credit balance (1 credit = 1 second of output). Check it before dubbing\na long video; a 402 means not enough credits.\n\nLanguage codes come from `GET https://dublab.app/api/langs` (public, no auth): use the\n`code` field as `dest_lang` / `source_lang`.\n\n## 2. Create a dub\nEither upload a local file (multipart, up to 1 GB) or pass a public URL.\n```bash\ncurl -sS --max-time 900 -X POST https://dublab.app/api/v2/dubs \\\n  -H \"apikey: $DUBLAB_API_KEY\" \\\n  -F source_lang=en -F dest_lang=fr \\\n  -F \"file=@video.mp4;type=video/mp4\"\n```\n```bash\ncurl -sS -X POST https://dublab.app/api/v2/dubs \\\n  -H \"apikey: $DUBLAB_API_KEY\" -H ''Content-Type: application/json'' \\\n  -d ''{\"source_url\":\"https://example.com/video.mp4\",\"dest_lang\":\"fr\"}''\n```\nParameters: `dest_lang` (required), `source_lang` (default `auto`), `name`, `duration`,\n`is_studio_quality` (true = 2x credits). Returns the dub `id`.\n\n**One target language per call**: dubbing into 3 languages means 3 POSTs.\n\n## 3. Poll until done\n```bash\ncurl -sS https://dublab.app/api/v2/dubs/<id> -H \"apikey: $DUBLAB_API_KEY\"\n```\n`external_status_id`: 1 uploading, 2 in queue, 3 processing, 4 failed, 5 completed.\nPoll every ~30s and follow `progress_percentage`. On 4, read `external_error_message`.\n\n## 4. Collect the outputs\n`outputs` stays empty until status 5, then holds `translated_mp4`, `translated_mp3` and\n`translated_subtitle`, each with a `url` and a `download_url`. Those links are presigned\nand expire after roughly 1 hour, so download them right away or re-fetch the dub to get\nfresh ones.\n\n`GET /api/v2/dubs?page=1&page_size=20` lists past dubs, newest first.\n\n## Rules\n- Dubbing costs credits and takes minutes: confirm the video and the target languages\n  with the user before creating a dub, and never re-create a job just to retry a poll.\n- Set generous timeouts on uploads (`--max-time 900`); a slow upload is not a failure.","name":"dublab-usage","description":"How to dub videos with the DubLab API"}],"envKeys":[{"key":"DUBLAB_API_KEY","fromInput":"DUBLAB_API_KEY"}],"summary":"Dub videos into 90+ languages with AI voice cloning that keeps the original voice.","category":"marketing","mcpServers":[],"description":"DubLab is an AI video dubbing platform that translates videos into 92 languages while cloning the original speaker''s voice and preserving background music. It has no MCP server, so the agent drives its REST API directly to upload a video, poll the dubbing job and fetch the translated MP4, MP3 and subtitles."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.048675537,0.0018510818,-0.016860962,-0.0011749268,0.0011930466,-0.010192871,0.007499695,0.035308838,0.030639648,-0.009155273,0.017150879,-0.04498291,-0.040649414,-0.02243042,-0.027542114,0.039642334,-0.043518066,-0.016693115,0.00015282631,0.0018348694,0.020111084,-0.006275177,-0.010375977,0.011779785,0.036102295,-0.0231781,-0.0413208,-0.022781372,0.009262085,-