('excalidraw', 'Excalidraw', 'productivity', 'Create, read, and manage Excalidraw whiteboard scenes and collections in your Excalidraw Plus workspace.', '/services/excalidraw.svg', '{"name":"Excalidraw","slug":"excalidraw","inputs":[{"key":"API_KEY","help":"In Excalidraw Plus, open your workspace/profile Settings > API Keys and create a public API key with the permissions you need. The key is shown only once, so copy it immediately. Requires an Excalidraw Plus account.","type":"password","label":"Excalidraw Plus API Key","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"excalidraw_..."}],"skills":[{"body":"# Excalidraw\n\nUse the `excalidraw_*` tools to work with your Excalidraw Plus whiteboards.\n\n- The server is the official Excalidraw+ hosted MCP at https://api.excalidraw.com/api/v1/mcp (Streamable HTTP).\n- Auth is a single Bearer API key created in your Excalidraw Plus workspace/profile Settings > API Keys.\n- Which tools are available depends on the permissions granted to your API key (they mirror the public REST API route permissions).\n\n## Typical flow\n1. List available tools to see what your key can access (e.g. scenes/collections operations).\n2. Read or list existing whiteboards/collections before modifying them.\n3. Create or update scenes as requested, then confirm the resulting IDs/URLs back to the user.\n\nIf a tool returns a permissions error, the API key likely lacks the required scope — ask the user to recreate the key with broader permissions in Excalidraw Plus settings.","name":"excalidraw-usage","description":"How to use the Excalidraw MCP tools to work with whiteboards and collections."}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Create, read, and manage Excalidraw whiteboard scenes and collections in your Excalidraw Plus workspace.","category":"productivity","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://api.excalidraw.com/api/v1/mcp","args":[],"name":"excalidraw","headers":{"Authorization":"Bearer ${input.API_KEY}"},"transport":"http"}],"description":"Connects the offic