('excel', 'Microsoft Excel', 'productivity', 'Read, write and structure data in Excel workbooks stored in OneDrive or SharePoint.', '/services/excel.png', '{"name":"Microsoft Excel","slug":"excel","skills":[{"body":"# Microsoft Excel\n\nEvery call works on a workbook item id. Find it with EXCEL_SEARCH_FILES (by name) or EXCEL_LIST_FILES (by folder), then list its tabs with EXCEL_LIST_WORKSHEETS. Ranges are A1 addresses without the sheet name (`A1:D50`); the worksheet goes in its own parameter.\n\nWhen you do not know where the data stops, EXCEL_GET_WORKSHEET_USED_RANGE returns the whole filled block. Otherwise read with EXCEL_GET_RANGE and write with EXCEL_UPDATE_RANGE (values or formulas, as a 2D array matching the address). EXCEL_CLEAR_RANGE empties cells, EXCEL_INSERT_RANGE makes room by shifting cells, EXCEL_SORT_RANGE sorts in place.\n\nMany business workbooks hold their data in tables. EXCEL_LIST_TABLES finds them, EXCEL_LIST_TABLE_COLUMNS and EXCEL_LIST_TABLE_ROWS read them, EXCEL_ADD_TABLE_ROW appends, which is the safe way to log new records because the table grows with formulas and formatting. EXCEL_ADD_TABLE turns a range into a table.\n\nStructure and output: EXCEL_CREATE_WORKBOOK for a new file, EXCEL_UPLOAD_WORKBOOK to import one from a URL, EXCEL_ADD_WORKSHEET, EXCEL_UPDATE_WORKSHEET and EXCEL_DELETE_WORKSHEET for tabs, EXCEL_ADD_CHART for a chart, EXCEL_EXPORT_WORKBOOK_TO_PDF to share a snapshot.\n\nWorkbooks living in a SharePoint site take a site id instead: use EXCEL_LIST_SHAREPOINT_WORKSHEETS, EXCEL_GET_SHAREPOINT_RANGE and EXCEL_UPDATE_SHAREPOINT_RANGE.\n\nWrites overwrite silently and colleagues may have the file open. Read the range first and confirm with the user before replacing data you did not write.","name":"excel-usage","description":"How to use Microsoft Excel tools"}],"summary":"Read, write and structure data in Excel workbooks stored in OneDrive or SharePoint.","category":"productivity","authMethods":[{"id":"composio","kind":"composio","label":"Connect with Microsoft","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"composio":{"toolkit":"excel","allowedTools":["EXCEL_SEARCH_FILES","EXCEL_LIST_FILES","EXCEL_CREATE_WORKBOOK","EXCEL_UPLOAD_WORKBOOK","EXCEL_LIST_WORKSHEETS","EXCEL_ADD_WORKSHEET","EXCEL_UPDATE_WORKSHEET","EXCEL_DELETE_WORKSHEET","EXCEL_GET_WORKSHEET_USED_RANGE","EXCEL_GET_RANGE","EXCEL_UPDATE_RANGE","EXCEL_CLEAR_RANGE","EXCEL_INSERT_RANGE","EXCEL_SORT_RANGE","EXCEL_LIST_TABLES","EXCEL_ADD_TABLE","EXCEL_LIST_TABLE_COLUMNS","EXCEL_LIST_TABLE_ROWS","EXCEL_ADD_TABLE_ROW","EXCEL_DELETE_TABLE_ROW","EXCEL_ADD_CHART","EXCEL_EXPORT_WORKBOOK_TO_PDF","EXCEL_LIST_SHAREPOINT_WORKSHEETS","EXCEL_GET_SHAREPOINT_RANGE","EXCEL_UPDATE_SHAREPOINT_RANGE","EXCEL_WHO_AM_I"],"authConfigId":""},"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"${LUMVIKA_HUB_BASE_URL}/api/mcp/composio/excel","args":[],"name":"excel","headers":{"x-lumvika-key":"${LUMVIKA_API_KEY}","x-lumvika-agent":"${agent.id}"},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":true}],"description":"Excel in one click: sign in with Microsoft and your agent can find workbooks, read ranges, write cells, append table rows, add sheets and charts, and export to PDF. The connection is brokered by Composio, so there is no Azure app registration and no token to paste. Works on workbooks in OneDrive and SharePoint, not on local files."}'::jsonb, false, false, '[-0.025146484,-0.001004219,0.029769897,0.020126343,0.045837402,-0.021972656,0.037139893,0.045959473,8.690357e-05,0.00762558,0.0023422241,-0.0126953125,0.0071983337,0.011459351,-0.015960693,0.06161499,0.0009713173,-0.0206604,0.004634857,0.021636963,0.01651001,0.019180298,0.005924225,0.06085205,-0.023529053,0.027328491,-0.082458496,0.012199402,-0.008728027,-0.051940918,-0.0074768066,-0.027297974,0.037322998,0.049591064,0.027389526,-0.014778137,0.014434814,0.07244873,0.024475098,-0.0010032654,0.0026226044,0.044036865,0.013916016,0.04611206,0.038513184,0.0063171387,-0.04437256,-0.04324341,0.023483276,0.00051927567,-0.0031929016,0.027999878,-0.0006995201,-