('fish-audio', 'Fish Audio', 'productivity', 'Generate speech, clone voices and transcribe audio with Fish Audio.', '/services/fish-audio.svg', '{"name":"Fish Audio","slug":"fish-audio","inputs":[],"skills":[{"body":"# Fish Audio\n\nUse the Fish Audio tools to browse the voice library, generate speech and transcribe audio.\n\n## Generating speech\n\nSearch the voice library first and pick a voice that matches the tone the user asked for, then generate. Reuse the same voice across a series so the narration stays consistent.\n\nText can carry inline audio tags to control delivery, e.g. `[whispering]`, `[excited]`, `[laughing]`. Use them sparingly and only where the script calls for a shift in tone.\n\nGenerated audio is returned as a permanent URL. Give that URL back to the user rather than describing the file.\n\n## Transcribing\n\nLocal files are uploaded temporarily and deleted after 7 days. Transcription also reports detected emotion, which is useful when analysing a recording rather than just reading it.\n\n## Credits\n\nCalls consume the user''s Fish Audio plan credits. Confirm before generating long scripts or regenerating a batch.","name":"fish-audio-usage","description":"How to use Fish Audio tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Generate speech, clone voices and transcribe audio with Fish Audio.","category":"productivity","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://api.fish.audio/mcp","args":[],"name":"fish-audio","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"description":"Connects Fish Audio''s hosted MCP server. Your agent can browse the voice library, turn text into natural-sounding speech with emotion tags, and transcribe audio files. You sign in with your Fish Audio account; no key to paste. Usage draws from your Fish Audio plan credits."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.006225586,0.019607544,0.010932922,-0.007270813,-0.011154175,-0.025299072,-0.02911377,0.03805542,0.009513855,-0.040130615,0.034332275,-0.014289856,-0.0043792725,0.0007715225,-0.008155823,0.023925781,-0