('getxapi', 'GetXAPI', 'marketing', 'Read and post on X (Twitter) — search tweets, users, followers, DMs and articles — through GetXAPI''s pay-per-call API.', '/services/getxapi.png', '{"name":"GetXAPI","slug":"getxapi","inputs":[{"key":"GETXAPI_KEY","help":"Sign up at getxapi.com (Google or email) and generate an API key from your dashboard. Free starter credits, no card required.","type":"password","label":"GetXAPI API key","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"get-x-api-…"},{"key":"X_AUTH_TOKEN","help":"Optional. The auth_token cookie of the X account the agent should act as. Required only for write tools (post, reply, like, retweet, DM, articles, profile) — read tools work without it.","type":"password","label":"X auth_token cookie","secret":true,"required":false},{"key":"X_CT0","help":"Optional. The ct0 cookie of the same X account. Improves reliability of write calls on some accounts.","type":"password","label":"X ct0 cookie","secret":true,"required":false}],"skills":[{"body":"# GetXAPI (X / Twitter)\n\nGetXAPI is an independent third-party API for X (Twitter), billed per call (~$0.001). The MCP server runs locally over stdio and exposes 47 tools.\n\n## Read tools (GETXAPI_KEY only)\n- Tweets: `advanced_search_tweets` (supports X search operators), `get_tweet_detail`, `get_tweet_replies`, `get_article`.\n- Users: `search_users`, `get_user_info`, `get_user_info_by_id`, `get_user_about`, `get_user_followers`, `get_user_following`, `get_verified_followers`, `get_followers_you_know`, `check_follow_relationship`, `get_user_affiliates`.\n- Timelines: `get_user_tweets`, `get_user_tweets_and_replies`, `get_user_mentions`, `get_user_likes`, `get_user_media`, `get_list_members`.\n\n## Write and private tools (also need X_AUTH_TOKEN)\n- Posting: `create_tweet`, `delete_tweet`, `upload_media`, `favorite_tweet`, `retweet_tweet`, `bookmark_tweet`, `unbookmark_tweet`.\n- Own account: `get_home_timeline`, `list_bookmarks`, `search_bookmarks`, `update_profile`, `update_avatar`, `update_banner`.\n- DMs: `list_direct_messages`, `get_direct_message_conversation`, `send_direct_message`.\n- Articles: `create_article`, `update_article`, `publish_article`, `unpublish_article`, `list_articles`, `delete_article`.\n- Account: `get_account_info` (GetXAPI credit balance), `get_payment_history`.\n\nIf a write tool fails with an auth error, X_AUTH_TOKEN is missing or expired — tell the user to update it in the service settings.\n\n## Rules\n- Never call `x_login`: it would pass the X password through the model''s context. Credentials are supplied as environment variables instead.\n- Every tool call costs credits. Avoid redundant calls, prefer one well-formed search over several broad ones, and stop paginating once you have enough results.\n- Confirm the exact text with the user before posting, replying, or sending a DM from their account.","name":"getxapi-usage","description":"How to use GetXAPI''s X (Twitter) tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Read and post on X (Twitter) — search tweets, users, followers, DMs and articles — through GetXAPI''s pay-per-call API.","category":"marketing","mcpServers":[{"env":{"X_CT0":"${input.X_CT0}","GETXAPI_KEY":"${input.GETXAPI_KEY}","X_AUTH_TOKEN":"${input.X_AUTH_TOKEN}"},"args":["-y","@getxapi/mcp@latest"],"name":"getxapi","command":"npx","headers":{},"transport":"stdio"}],"description":"GetXAPI is an independent third-party X (Twitter) API: no X developer account, no subscription, $0.001 per call. Its official MCP server runs locally over stdio and exposes 47 tools. Read tools only need your GetXAPI key; write tools (post, like, retweet, DM, articles, profile) also need the auth_token cookie of the X account to act as."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.008239746,0.024673462,0.03717041,-0.003107071,-0.0042800903,-0.034179688,-0.03390503,0.011116028,0.032165527,-0.015563965,0.030929565,-0.035461426,-0.026473999,0.03829956,-0.002313614,0.02532959,-0.034942627,-0.0118255615,-0.0027008057,0.058013916,0.0047721863,0.047