('gmail', 'Gmail', 'productivity', 'Read, search, send and organize email in the user''s Gmail account.', '/services/gmail.svg', '{"name":"Gmail","slug":"gmail","skills":[{"body":"# Gmail\n\nSearch the mailbox with GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS, which takes Gmail query syntax (`from:alice is:unread newer_than:7d`). Open one message with GMAIL_FETCH_MESSAGE_BY_MESSAGE_ID, a whole conversation with GMAIL_FETCH_MESSAGE_BY_THREAD_ID, and browse conversations with GMAIL_LIST_THREADS.\n\nSend with GMAIL_SEND_EMAIL, answer inside a conversation with GMAIL_REPLY_TO_THREAD (never invent a new subject, the thread carries it), and pass a message along with GMAIL_FORWARD_MESSAGE. When the user should review before anything leaves, write a draft with GMAIL_CREATE_EMAIL_DRAFT, revise it with GMAIL_UPDATE_DRAFT, and send it with GMAIL_SEND_DRAFT. Always confirm recipients before sending.\n\nOrganize with GMAIL_LIST_LABELS, GMAIL_CREATE_LABEL, GMAIL_ADD_LABEL_TO_EMAIL for one message and GMAIL_MODIFY_THREAD_LABELS for a whole thread. GMAIL_MOVE_TO_TRASH is the only deletion available and it is recoverable. Attachments come from GMAIL_GET_ATTACHMENT, the signed-in address from GMAIL_GET_PROFILE, and a recipient''s address can be looked up with GMAIL_SEARCH_PEOPLE.","name":"gmail-usage","description":"How to use Gmail tools"}],"summary":"Read, search, send and organize email in the user''s Gmail account.","category":"productivity","authMethods":[{"id":"composio","kind":"composio","label":"Connect with Google","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"composio":{"toolkit":"gmail","allowedTools":["GMAIL_FETCH_EMAILS","GMAIL_FETCH_MESSAGE_BY_MESSAGE_ID","GMAIL_FETCH_MESSAGE_BY_THREAD_ID","GMAIL_LIST_THREADS","GMAIL_SEND_EMAIL","GMAIL_REPLY_TO_THREAD","GMAIL_FORWARD_MESSAGE","GMAIL_CREATE_EMAIL_DRAFT","GMAIL_UPDATE_DRAFT","GMAIL_LIST_DRAFTS","GMAIL_SEND_DRAFT","GMAIL_GET_ATTACHMENT","GMAIL_LIST_LABELS","GMAIL_CREATE_LABEL","GMAIL_ADD_LABEL_TO_EMAIL","GMAIL_MODIFY_THREAD_LABELS","GMAIL_MOVE_TO_TRASH","GMAIL_GET_PRO