('gong', 'Gong', 'crm', 'Search Gong calls, read transcripts and summaries, and look up users, trackers and workspaces.', '/services/gong.png?tone=light', '{"name":"Gong","slug":"gong","inputs":[{"key":"GONG_ACCESS_KEY","help":"As a Gong technical admin: Company Settings > Ecosystem > API > Create. Copy the Access Key. See https://help.gong.io/docs/receive-access-to-the-api","type":"password","label":"Gong Access Key","secret":true,"required":true},{"key":"GONG_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET","help":"Shown once, on the same screen as the Access Key. Gong never reveals it again - if you lost it, create a new key pair.","type":"password","label":"Gong Access Key Secret","secret":true,"required":true}],"skills":[{"body":"# Gong\n\nGong is a revenue intelligence platform: it records, transcribes and analyses sales calls. The MCP server runs locally over stdio and talks to Gong''s REST API with the workspace Access Key and Secret.\n\n## Calls\n- `list_calls` - list calls in a date range; the entry point when the user has no specific call in mind.\n- `get_call` - full metadata for one call (participants, duration, direction, CRM links).\n- `get_call_summary` - Gong''s AI summary of a call. Prefer it over the raw transcript when the user wants the gist.\n- `get_call_transcript` - full transcript with speakers. Long: only fetch it when quotes or details actually matter.\n\n## Search\n- `search_calls` - flexible search with filters (date range, workspace, participants).\n- `search_calls_by_account` / `search_calls_by_opportunity` - all calls tied to a CRM account or opportunity. Use these for account reviews and deal post-mortems.\n- `search_transcripts` - search across what was actually said, not just call metadata.\n\n## Org and context\n- `get_trackers` - the workspace''s configured keyword trackers (competitors, objections, pricing).\n- `list_workspaces` - resolve the workspace id when the org has several.\n- `list_library_folders` / `get_library_folder_calls` - curated call libraries (onboarding, best calls).\n\n## Users\n- `list_users`, `search_users`, `get_user` - resolve a rep''s name to a Gong user id before filtering calls by owner.\n\n## Rules\n- Gong rate-limits to 3 requests per second and 10,000 calls per day for the whole company. Do not paginate further than needed, and prefer one narrow search over several broad ones.\n- Calls marked private in Gong are excluded from the API - if an expected call is missing, that is usually why.\n- Transcripts contain what customers actually said. Quote them internally, but never republish them externally without checking with the user first.\n- The API is read-only: you can analyse calls, not modify them.","name":"gong-usage","description":"How to use Gong tools"}],"envKeys":[{"key":"GONG_ACCESS_KEY","fromInput":"GONG_ACCESS_KEY"},{"key":"GONG_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET","fromInput":"GONG_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET"}],"summary":"Search Gong calls, read transcripts and summaries, and look up users, trackers and workspaces.","category":"crm","mcpServers":[{"env":{"GONG_ACCESS_KEY":"${input.GONG_ACCESS_KEY}","GONG_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET":"${input.GONG_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET}"},"args":["-y","gongio-mcp@latest"],"name":"gong","command":"npx","headers":{},"transport":"stdio"}],"authMethods":[],"description":"Gong is a revenue intelligence platform that records and analyses sales calls. This connector runs the community gongio-mcp server locally over stdio against Gong''s public REST API, so agents can list and search calls, pull transcripts and summaries, search across transcripts, and resolve users, trackers and library folders. Authenticates with a Gong Access Key and Access Key Secret created by a Gong technical admin. Gong''s own hosted MCP server is not usable here because it requires an OAuth client that each customer registers manually."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.035461426,0.029678345,0.06390381,0.0028533936,-0.0060539246,-0.021591187,-0.018692017,0.06323242,0.033996582,-0.04196167,0.047302246,-0.013832092,-0.014533997,0.