('google-analytics', 'Google Analytics', 'analytics', 'Query GA4 traffic, conversions and realtime reports.', '/services/google-analytics.svg', '{"name":"Google Analytics","slug":"google-analytics","skills":[{"body":"# Google Analytics (GA4)\n\nStart with GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_LIST_ACCOUNT_SUMMARIES to get the accounts and their properties, or GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_LIST_PROPERTIES_FILTERED to narrow them down. Every report needs a numeric property id. GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_GET_PROPERTY returns the timezone and currency of a property, which you need to read its numbers correctly.\n\nGOOGLE_ANALYTICS_RUN_REPORT is the workhorse: it takes dimensions, metrics and a date range. GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_BATCH_RUN_REPORTS runs several in one call, GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_RUN_PIVOT_REPORT cross-tabulates, GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_RUN_FUNNEL_REPORT measures a step-by-step funnel and GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_RUN_REALTIME_REPORT covers the last 30 minutes.\n\nGA4 rejects incompatible dimension and metric pairs. When a report errors, list what the property actually exposes with GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_GET_METADATA and test the combination with GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_CHECK_COMPATIBILITY rather than guessing again.\n\nConfiguration, when the user asks what is being tracked: GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_LIST_DATA_STREAMS, GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_LIST_KEY_EVENTS, GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_LIST_CONVERSION_EVENTS, GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_LIST_AUDIENCES, GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_LIST_CUSTOM_DIMENSIONS and GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_LIST_CUSTOM_METRICS.\n\nThis connector is read-only. Report the date range and property alongside any figure you give.","name":"google-analytics-usage","description":"How to use Google Analytics tools"}],"summary":"Query GA4 traffic, conversions and realtime reports.","category":"analytics","authMethods":[{"id":"composio","kind":"composio","label":"Connect with Google","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"composio":{"toolkit":"google_analytics","allowedTools":["GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_LIST_ACCOUNT_SUMMARIES","GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_LIST_PROPERTIES_FILTERED","GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_GET_PROPERTY","