('google-bigquery', 'Google BigQuery', 'dev', 'Explore BigQuery datasets and run SQL queries.', '/services/google-bigquery.svg', '{"name":"Google BigQuery","slug":"google-bigquery","skills":[{"body":"# Google BigQuery\n\nExplore before querying: GOOGLEBIGQUERY_LIST_PROJECTS, then GOOGLEBIGQUERY_LIST_DATASETS, GOOGLEBIGQUERY_LIST_TABLES and GOOGLEBIGQUERY_GET_TABLE_SCHEMA. Never write SQL against columns you have not read in a schema. GOOGLEBIGQUERY_LIST_TABLE_DATA reads rows without running a query at all, which is free and enough to sample a table.\n\nGOOGLEBIGQUERY_QUERY runs standard SQL synchronously and is the tool for almost every request. Fully qualify tables as `project.dataset.table` and keep a LIMIT on exploratory queries: BigQuery bills by bytes scanned, and `select *` on a large table is expensive. GOOGLEBIGQUERY_GET_DATASET returns a dataset''s location, which must match the one your query runs in.\n\nFor long jobs, GOOGLEBIGQUERY_INSERT_JOB starts one asynchronously, GOOGLEBIGQUERY_GET_JOB polls it, GOOGLEBIGQUERY_GET_QUERY_RESULTS reads the rows, GOOGLEBIGQUERY_LIST_JOBS shows recent history and GOOGLEBIGQUERY_CANCEL_JOB stops one.\n\nWrites: GOOGLEBIGQUERY_CREATE_DATASET, GOOGLEBIGQUERY_CREATE_TABLE, GOOGLEBIGQUERY_PATCH_TABLE for the schema or description, GOOGLEBIGQUERY_INSERT_ALL to stream rows in and GOOGLEBIGQUERY_DELETE_TABLE. Dropping a table takes its data with it, so confirm with the user first.","name":"google-bigquery-usage","description":"How to use Google BigQuery tools"}],"summary":"Explore BigQuery datasets and run SQL queries.","category":"dev","authMethods":[{"id":"composio","kind":"composio","label":"Connect with Google","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"composio":{"toolkit":"googlebigquery","allowedTools":["GOOGLEBIGQUERY_LIST_PROJECTS","GOOGLEBIGQUERY_LIST_DATASETS","GOOGLEBIGQUERY_GET_DATASET","GOOGLEBIGQUERY_LIST_TABLES","GOOGLEBIGQUERY_GET_TABLE_SCHEMA","GOOGLEBIGQUERY_LIST_TABLE_DATA","GOOGLEBIGQUERY_QUERY","GOOGLEBIGQUERY_INSERT_JOB"