('google-calendar', 'Google Calendar', 'productivity', 'Read the user''s calendars, find free slots and manage events.', '/services/google-calendar.svg', '{"name":"Google Calendar","slug":"google-calendar","skills":[{"body":"# Google Calendar\n\nCall GOOGLECALENDAR_GET_CURRENT_DATE_TIME first whenever the user says \"tomorrow\", \"next week\" or any relative date. Never compute a date from memory.\n\nGOOGLECALENDAR_LIST_CALENDARS shows the calendars the account can see. GOOGLECALENDAR_EVENTS_LIST reads one calendar over a time range, GOOGLECALENDAR_EVENTS_LIST_ALL_CALENDARS reads them all at once, and GOOGLECALENDAR_FIND_EVENT searches by text. GOOGLECALENDAR_EVENTS_GET fetches a single event by id, and GOOGLECALENDAR_EVENTS_INSTANCES expands a recurring one. GOOGLECALENDAR_FIND_FREE_SLOTS is what you use to propose a meeting time.\n\nCreate with GOOGLECALENDAR_CREATE_EVENT, or GOOGLECALENDAR_QUICK_ADD when the user gave one natural sentence. Editing requires the event id, so search first: GOOGLECALENDAR_PATCH_EVENT changes a few fields, GOOGLECALENDAR_UPDATE_EVENT replaces the event, GOOGLECALENDAR_EVENTS_MOVE sends it to another calendar and GOOGLECALENDAR_REMOVE_ATTENDEE drops one guest. GOOGLECALENDAR_DELETE_EVENT cancels it.\n\nAlways state the timezone you used, and confirm with the user before touching an event with other attendees, since they all get notified.","name":"google-calendar-usage","description":"How to use Google Calendar tools"}],"summary":"Read the user''s calendars, find free slots and manage events.","category":"productivity","authMethods":[{"id":"composio","kind":"composio","label":"Connect with Google","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"composio":{"toolkit":"googlecalendar","allowedTools":["GOOGLECALENDAR_GET_CURRENT_DATE_TIME","GOOGLECALENDAR_LIST_CALENDARS","GOOGLECALENDAR_GET_CALENDAR","GOOGLECALENDAR_CREATE_CALENDAR","GOOGLECALENDAR_EVENTS_LIST","GOOGLECALENDAR_EVENTS_LIST_ALL_CALENDARS","GOOGLECALENDAR_FIND_EVENT","GOOGLECALENDAR_EVENTS_GET","GO