('google-drive', 'Google Drive', 'productivity', 'Search, read, create and share files in Google Drive.', '/services/google-drive.svg', '{"name":"Google Drive","slug":"google-drive","skills":[{"body":"# Google Drive\n\nGOOGLEDRIVE_FIND_FILE is the main entry point: it takes Drive query syntax (`name contains ''report'' and mimeType = ''application/pdf''`) and returns file ids. GOOGLEDRIVE_FIND_FOLDER does the same for folders, and GOOGLEDRIVE_GET_FILE_METADATA confirms the mime type, parents and trashed state of an id before you act on it.\n\nRead a binary or plain file with GOOGLEDRIVE_DOWNLOAD_FILE. For Docs, Sheets and Slides use GOOGLEDRIVE_EXPORT_GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_FILE with the target mime type instead, since Workspace files have no raw bytes.\n\nCreate text files with GOOGLEDRIVE_CREATE_FILE_FROM_TEXT, folders with GOOGLEDRIVE_CREATE_FOLDER, and bring content in with GOOGLEDRIVE_UPLOAD_FILE (under 5MB) or GOOGLEDRIVE_UPLOAD_FROM_URL. GOOGLEDRIVE_EDIT_FILE overwrites a file''s content, GOOGLEDRIVE_UPDATE_FILE_PUT changes its metadata such as the name, GOOGLEDRIVE_MOVE_FILE reparents it and GOOGLEDRIVE_COPY_FILE_ADVANCED duplicates it.\n\nGOOGLEDRIVE_TRASH_FILE is the only removal available and it is recoverable. Confirm the target file with the user before overwriting or trashing anything.\n\nSharing goes through GOOGLEDRIVE_LIST_PERMISSIONS, GOOGLEDRIVE_CREATE_PERMISSION and GOOGLEDRIVE_DELETE_PERMISSION. Never widen access to `anyone` unless the user asked for a public link. GOOGLEDRIVE_LIST_SHARED_DRIVES lists the shared drives the account belongs to.","name":"google-drive-usage","description":"How to use Google Drive tools"}],"summary":"Search, read, create and share files in Google Drive.","category":"productivity","authMethods":[{"id":"composio","kind":"composio","label":"Connect with Google","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"composio":{"toolkit":"googledrive","allowedTools":["GOOGLEDRIVE_FIND_FILE","GOOGLEDRIVE_FIND_FOLDER","GOOGLEDRIVE_GET_FILE_METADATA","GOOGLE