('google-maps', 'Google Maps', 'productivity', 'Search places, resolve Maps links, compute routes and look up weather with Google Maps data.', '/services/google-maps.svg', '{"name":"Google Maps","slug":"google-maps","inputs":[{"key":"api_key","help":"Google Cloud Console -> APIs & Services -> Library -> enable Maps Grounding Lite API (mapstools.googleapis.com), then Credentials -> Create Credentials -> API Key. The API must be enabled on both the project and the key.","type":"password","label":"Google Maps API key","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"AIza..."}],"skills":[{"body":"# Google Maps (Maps Grounding Lite)\n\nGrounded Google Maps data over the official hosted MCP server.\n\n## Tools\n- `search_places` — find businesses, addresses, points of interest. Put the full intent in `text_query` (\"date night restaurants in Chicago\", \"Google Store Mountain View opening hours\"). Optional `location_bias` circle (center lat/lng + radius_meters) to prioritize an area.\n- `resolve_names` — turn up to 20 place names or addresses into canonical Place IDs.\n- `resolve_maps_urls` — extract Place IDs from up to 20 Google Maps share links.\n- `compute_routes` — distance and duration between an origin and a destination, DRIVE or WALK.\n- `lookup_weather` — current conditions, hourly and daily forecasts for a location.\n\n## Tips\n- Resolve a name to a Place ID first when you need to chain several calls on the same place.\n- `compute_routes` returns distance and duration only: no turn-by-turn steps, no live traffic.\n- Always cite the Google Maps link returned by `search_places` when reporting a place to the user.","name":"google-maps-usage","description":"How to use Google Maps tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Search places, resolve Maps links, compute routes and look up weather with Google Maps data.","category":"productivity","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mapstools.googleapis.com/mcp","args":[],"name":"google-maps","headers":{"X-Goog-Api-Key":"${input.api_