('google-sheets', 'Google Sheets', 'productivity', 'Read, write and reshape data in Google Sheets spreadsheets.', '/services/google-sheets.svg', '{"name":"Google Sheets","slug":"google-sheets","skills":[{"body":"# Google Sheets\n\nFind a spreadsheet with GOOGLESHEETS_SEARCH_SPREADSHEETS, then get its structure with GOOGLESHEETS_GET_SPREADSHEET_INFO or the tab names alone with GOOGLESHEETS_GET_SHEET_NAMES. Every range is A1 notation and carries its tab (`Sheet1!A1:D50`).\n\nRead one range with GOOGLESHEETS_VALUES_GET and several at once with GOOGLESHEETS_BATCH_GET. Write over a range with GOOGLESHEETS_VALUES_UPDATE, over several with GOOGLESHEETS_UPDATE_VALUES_BATCH, and add rows at the bottom with GOOGLESHEETS_SPREADSHEETS_VALUES_APPEND. GOOGLESHEETS_UPSERT_ROWS updates rows matching a key and appends the rest, which is what you want for a sync. GOOGLESHEETS_CLEAR_VALUES empties cells while keeping their formatting.\n\nGOOGLESHEETS_LOOKUP_SPREADSHEET_ROW finds the row whose cell exactly matches a value, and GOOGLESHEETS_AGGREGATE_COLUMN_DATA sums or averages a column filtered on another one, which avoids reading the whole sheet.\n\nStructure: GOOGLESHEETS_CREATE_GOOGLE_SHEET1 for a new spreadsheet, GOOGLESHEETS_ADD_SHEET and GOOGLESHEETS_DELETE_SHEET for tabs, GOOGLESHEETS_INSERT_DIMENSION and GOOGLESHEETS_DELETE_DIMENSION for rows and columns. Presentation: GOOGLESHEETS_FORMAT_CELL, GOOGLESHEETS_SORT_RANGE, GOOGLESHEETS_FIND_REPLACE.\n\nWrites overwrite silently. Read the range first and confirm with the user before replacing data you did not write.","name":"google-sheets-usage","description":"How to use Google Sheets tools"}],"summary":"Read, write and reshape data in Google Sheets spreadsheets.","category":"productivity","authMethods":[{"id":"composio","kind":"composio","label":"Connect with Google","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"composio":{"toolkit":"googlesheets","allowedTools":["GOOGLESHEETS_SEARCH_SPREADSHEETS","GOOGLESHEETS_GET_SPREADSHEET_INFO","GOOGLESHEETS_GET