('gusto', 'Gusto', 'productivity', 'Query your Gusto payroll, employee, and HR data using natural language through Gusto''s official MCP server.', '/services/gusto.svg', '{"name":"Gusto","slug":"gusto","inputs":[],"skills":[{"body":"# Gusto\n\nGusto''s MCP server gives read-only access to your Gusto account: payroll schedules, employee records, headcount, and HR data.\n\n## Connecting\n\nAuthentication uses OAuth 2.0. On first use a browser window opens where you sign in to Gusto and click Authorize, then choose which categories of data the assistant may access. No API key to paste.\n\n## Usage\n\n- Ask about upcoming payroll runs and pay schedules.\n- Look up employee records and headcount.\n- Query HR information without logging into the Gusto dashboard.\n\nAll tools are read-only, so the assistant cannot change payroll or employee data.\n\n## Security\n\nUse Gusto in an isolated client session. Do not connect other MCP servers to the same session to avoid leaking payroll data to another service.","name":"gusto-usage","description":"How to use the Gusto MCP tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Query your Gusto payroll, employee, and HR data using natural language through Gusto''s official MCP server.","category":"productivity","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.api.gusto.com","args":[],"name":"gusto","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"description":"Gusto is a payroll, benefits, and HR platform for small and medium businesses. Its official hosted MCP server exposes read-only access to payroll schedules, employee records, headcount, and HR information. Connect via browser-based OAuth sign-in, then select which data categories the assistant may access."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.014007568,0.024810791,0.019760132,0.01651001,-0.038238525,-0.032592773,0.0047073364,0.07305908,0.017288208,-0.04989624,0.042663574,0.004711151,0.011360168,-0.024917603,-0.0026397705,0.06298828,-0.019927979,-0.02305603,-0.01876831,0.03741455,0.017913818,0.06921387,-0.02734375,