('ifttt', 'IFTTT', 'productivity', 'Trigger and automate 1,000+ connected apps and services from your AI assistant via IFTTT''s MCP server.', '/services/ifttt.svg?tone=dark', '{"name":"IFTTT","slug":"ifttt","inputs":[],"skills":[{"body":"# IFTTT MCP\n\nIFTTT MCP lets you reach into your connected IFTTT services and take action across 1,000+ integrations.\n\n## Auth\n\nOn first use the server requires authentication via a standard browser OAuth flow tied to your IFTTT account. Complete the sign-in when prompted; no API key is needed.\n\n## What you can do\n\n- Run actions on any connected service in real time (e.g. send a Slack message, log a task, post an update).\n- Search IFTTT''s library of pre-built Applets and enable them without leaving the conversation.\n- Describe an automation in plain language and have it built as an IFTTT Applet.\n- Ask which IFTTT services you have connected to confirm the connection.\n\n## Tips\n\n- Make sure the relevant services are already connected in your IFTTT account before asking the assistant to act on them.\n- Actions execute immediately on your live accounts, so confirm intent before triggering irreversible operations.","name":"ifttt-usage","description":"How to use IFTTT MCP tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Trigger and automate 1,000+ connected apps and services from your AI assistant via IFTTT''s MCP server.","category":"productivity","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://ifttt.com/mcp","args":[],"name":"ifttt","oauth":{},"transport":"http"}],"description":"IFTTT MCP gives AI assistants direct access to your connected IFTTT services and Applets. Ask it to run actions, trigger automations, or build new Applets across 1,000+ integrations in real time. Authentication is handled through a standard browser OAuth sign-in to your IFTTT account."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.03427124,-0.042053223,0.0236969,-0.007335663,0.012397766,-0.056732178,0.05984497,0.068481445,0.0017337799,0.015823364,-0.013832092,0.0053215027,-0.01876831,-0.