('instagram', 'Instagram', 'marketing', 'Publish posts, carousels, Reels and stories, read insights, and answer comments and DMs on your Instagram professional account.', '/services/instagram.svg', '{"name":"Instagram","slug":"instagram","skills":[{"body":"# Instagram\n\nYou act as the connected Instagram business or creator account. Call `instagram_INSTAGRAM_GET_USER_INFO` with `ig_user_id: \"me\"` first: most tools need the numeric account id it returns as `ig_user_id`.\n\n## Publishing\n\nPublishing always takes two steps: create a container, then publish it.\n\n1. Create the container:\n   - Single photo: `instagram_INSTAGRAM_POST_IG_USER_MEDIA` with `image_url` (a public JPEG URL).\n   - Reel: same tool with `media_type: \"REELS\"` and `video_url` (a public MP4 URL).\n   - Story: same tool with `media_type: \"STORIES\"` and an image or video URL.\n   - Carousel (2 to 10 items): `instagram_INSTAGRAM_CREATE_CAROUSEL_CONTAINER` with `child_image_urls` / `child_video_urls` and the caption.\n2. Publish with `instagram_INSTAGRAM_POST_IG_USER_MEDIA_PUBLISH`, passing the container id as `creation_id`. It waits for videos to finish processing.\n\nMedia must be reachable at a public URL Meta can fetch. Containers expire within 24 hours, so publish right after creating. Instagram caps posts per 24 hours: check `instagram_INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_USER_CONTENT_PUBLISHING_LIMIT` before publishing several in a row. Posts cannot be scheduled nor edited after publishing, apart from turning comments on or off with `instagram_INSTAGRAM_SET_MEDIA_COMMENT_ENABLED`.\n\nAlways show the user the exact media and caption and wait for approval before publishing.\n\n## Reading and analytics\n\n`instagram_INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_USER_MEDIA` lists the published posts, `instagram_INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_MEDIA` reads one (use the numeric media id, not the shortcode from the post URL), `instagram_INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_MEDIA_CHILDREN` lists the items of a carousel. `instagram_INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_USER_STORIES` lists the active stories, `instagram_INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_USER_TAGS` the posts the account is tagged in.\n\n`instagram_INSTAGRAM_GET_USER_INSIGHTS` returns account metrics (reach, views, followers), `instagram_INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_MEDIA_INSIGHTS` the metrics of one post (views, reach, likes, comments, saved, shares). Insights can come back empty on small accounts or very recent posts: say so instead of retrying.\n\n## Comments\n\nRead with `instagram_INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_MEDIA_COMMENTS` and `instagram_INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_COMMENT_REPLIES`. Reply with `instagram_INSTAGRAM_POST_IG_COMMENT_REPLIES`, comment on a post with `instagram_INSTAGRAM_POST_IG_MEDIA_COMMENTS`, answer a mention with `instagram_INSTAGRAM_POST_IG_USER_MENTIONS`. Draft replies for the user''s approval unless they asked you to answer on your own. Use `instagram_INSTAGRAM_DELETE_COMMENT` only when the user asks for a deletion.\n\n## Direct messages\n\n`instagram_INSTAGRAM_LIST_ALL_CONVERSATIONS` (with `platform: \"instagram\"`) lists the threads, `instagram_INSTAGRAM_LIST_ALL_MESSAGES` reads one. Reply with `instagram_INSTAGRAM_SEND_TEXT_MESSAGE` or `instagram_INSTAGRAM_SEND_IMAGE`, using the recipient id from the conversation, never a username. You can only answer someone who wrote first, within Instagram''s messaging window: if the send fails with error subcode 2534022, tell the user and do not retry. Mark a thread read with `instagram_INSTAGRAM_MARK_SEEN`. Show the user every DM before sending unless they asked you to answer on your own.\n\n## Not available\n\nPersonal Instagram accounts, other people''s profiles and follower lists, starting a new DM thread, scheduling, editing a published caption, and ads are out of reach. Ads live in the Meta Ads app.","name":"instagram-usage","description":"How to use Instagram tools"}],"summary":"Publish posts, carousels, Reels and stories, read insights, and answer comments and DMs on your Instagram professional account.","category":"marketing","authMethods":[{"id":"composio","kind":"composio","label":"Connect with Instagram","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"composio":{"toolkit":"instagram","allowedTools":["INSTAGRAM_POST_IG_USER_MEDIA","INSTAGRAM_CREATE_CAROUSEL_CONTAINER","INSTAGRAM_POST_IG_USER_MEDIA_PUBLISH","INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_USER_CONTENT_PUBLISHING_LIMIT","INSTAGRAM_GET_USER_INFO","INSTAGRAM_GET_USER_INSIGHTS","INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_USER_MEDIA","INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_MEDIA","INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_MEDIA_CHILDREN","INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_MEDIA_INSIGHTS","INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_USER_STORIES","INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_USER_TAGS","INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_MEDIA_COMMENTS","INSTAGRAM_GET_IG_COMMENT_REPLIES","INSTAGRAM_POST_IG_MEDIA_COMMENTS","INSTAGRAM_POST_IG_COMMENT_REPLIES","INSTAGRAM_POST_IG_USER_MENTIONS","INSTAGRAM_DELETE_COMMENT","INSTAGRAM_SET_MEDIA_COMMENT_ENABLED","INSTAGRAM_LIST_ALL_CONVERSATIONS","INSTAGRAM_GET_CONVERSATION","INSTAGRAM_LIST_ALL_MESSAGES","INSTAGRAM_SEND_TEXT_MESSAGE","INSTAGRAM_SEND_IMAGE","INSTAGRAM_MARK_SEEN"],"authConfigId":""},"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"${LUMVIKA_HUB_BASE_URL}/api/mcp/composio/instagram","args":[],"name":"instagram","headers":{"x-lumvika-key":"${LUMVIKA_API_KEY}","x-lumvika-agent":"${agent.id}"},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":true}],"description":"Connect Instagram in one click. Lumvika brokers the connection through Composio and runs the Instagram calls for you: no developer app, no token to paste. Publish photos, carousels, Reels and stories, read account and post insights, reply to and moderate comments, and answer DMs. Works with Instagram business and creator accounts, not personal ones.","multiInstance":true}'::jsonb, true, false, '[0.006931305,0.0065689087,-0.023483276,-0.007801056,0.017456055,-0.06365967,0.015213013,0.011131287,0.00016570091,0.017044067,0.0019054413,-0.0059509277,-0.0015506744,0.018295288,0.0022640228,0.006298065,-0.047302246,0.019683838,0.03982544,0.07702637,-0.0038700104,0.0069389343,0.0012283325,0.051239014,0.00022232533,0.028366089,-0.08068848,-0.026489258,-0.013366699,-0.0019779205,0.007297516,-0.027374268,-0.00989