('intercom', 'Intercom', 'crm', 'Search and read Intercom conversations, contacts, and customer data through Intercom''s official hosted MCP server.', '/services/intercom.svg?tone=dark', '{"name":"Intercom","slug":"intercom","skills":[{"body":"# Intercom\n\nUse the `intercom_*` tools to search and read data from a connected Intercom workspace via Intercom''s official hosted MCP server.\n\n## What you can do\n- Search conversations using Intercom''s query DSL (by state, tag, author, date, keywords).\n- Look up contacts (users and leads) and companies.\n- Retrieve full conversation objects, including message parts, to answer support questions or summarize customer history.\n\n## Tips\n- The server is read-focused: use it to find and summarize customer context, not to mutate data.\n- Conversation search returns raw conversation objects; re-read the relevant parts before summarizing for the user.\n- Only US-hosted Intercom workspaces are supported. If tools return auth errors, verify the connection (OAuth sign-in) or that the Access Token is valid and has read scopes for users/companies and conversations.\n","name":"intercom-usage","description":"How to search and read Intercom conversations and contacts via the intercom_* MCP tools."}],"summary":"Search and read Intercom conversations, contacts, and customer data through Intercom''s official hosted MCP server.","category":"crm","authMethods":[{"id":"oauth","kind":"oauth","label":"Sign in with Intercom","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.intercom.com/mcp","args":[],"name":"intercom","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":true},{"id":"access-token","kind":"key","label":"Intercom Access Token","inputs":[{"key":"API_KEY","help":"Intercom Developer Hub > Your Apps > select your app > Configure > Authentication section (the Access Token). Also visible under Test & Publish > Your Workspaces. Requires a US-hosted workspace.","type":"password","label":"Intercom Access Token",