('kie-ai', 'Kie.ai', 'dev', 'Generate images, videos, music and speech with Veo 3, Nano Banana, Kling, Suno, Flux and more through one low-cost API.', '/services/kie-ai.png', '{"name":"Kie.ai","slug":"kie-ai","inputs":[{"key":"KIE_AI_API_KEY","help":"Create it at https://kie.ai/api-key","type":"password","label":"Kie.ai API key","secret":true,"required":true}],"skills":[{"body":"# Kie.ai\n\nKie.ai exposes one tool per media model: images (nano_banana_image, gpt_image_2, flux2_image, bytedance_seedream_image, midjourney_generate, qwen_image, z_image), video (veo3_generate_video, kling_video, bytedance_seedance_video, runway_aleph_video, wan_video, hailuo_video), audio (suno_generate_music, elevenlabs_tts, elevenlabs_ttsfx) and editing (topaz_upscale_image, recraft_remove_background, ideogram_reframe).\n\n## Workflow\n1. Not sure which model fits? Call list_models to search by capability.\n2. Input images or audio must be public URLs. For a local file, call upload_file (base64) first and pass the returned URL.\n3. Generation is asynchronous: the tool returns a task_id. Call wait_for_task (or poll get_task_status) until it succeeds, then read the output URLs.\n4. Output URLs expire: download the files you want to keep into the workspace.\n\n## Cost\nEvery generation spends the user''s Kie.ai credits, and video is the most expensive. Generate one variant first, and only batch or retry when the user asked for it.","name":"kie-ai-usage","description":"How to use the Kie.ai MCP tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Generate images, videos, music and speech with Veo 3, Nano Banana, Kling, Suno, Flux and more through one low-cost API.","category":"dev","mcpServers":[{"env":{"KIE_AI_API_KEY":"${input.KIE_AI_API_KEY}","KIE_AI_ALLOW_DIRECT_GENERATION":"true"},"args":["-y","@felores/kie-ai-mcp-server@5"],"name":"kie-ai","command":"npx","headers":{},"transport":"stdio"}],"description":"Kie.ai is a single API for state-of-the-art AI media models (Veo 3, Nano Banana, GPT Image 2, Kling,