('klubizz', 'Klubizz', 'marketing', 'Run your Klubizz community: publish posts, manage members and offers, schedule events and read revenue.', '/services/klubizz.png', '{"name":"Klubizz","slug":"klubizz","skills":[{"body":"# Klubizz\n\nThe connection carries one Klub: every tool acts on it and on no other. Call `me` first to see which Klub, which plan and which rate limit you have.\n\n## The shape of a Klub\n\n- A **space** holds posts or content. Its `accessType` is one of `free`, `tier`, `one_time`, `free_price`, `staff`.\n- A **tier** is an offer (subscription, one-off, lifetime, instalments) carrying one or more prices.\n- Spaces and space groups are born as drafts. Publishing is a second call with `isDraft: false`.\n\n## Rules the API enforces\n\n- **A member holds one tier at a time.** `tier_grant` replaces the tier they had, it never adds to it. Selling two things at once needs a bundle tier.\n- **Post bodies are HTML.** Newlines collapse at render, so write `<p>`, `<h3>`, `<strong>` — never plain text with `\\n`.\n- **There is no `post_update`.** Fixing a post means `post_create` then `post_delete`, and the delete is irreversible: recreate first, delete second.\n- **`tier_update` replaces the whole offer.** Send `prices` back every time or they are wiped. A tier''s type is immutable after creation.\n- A paid tier cannot move to `visibility: invite`. To pull it from sale, set `isActive: false`.\n- **A draft space group hides its spaces, even published ones.** Moving the default space into a draft group empties the sidebar for every member.\n- Slug, currency, logo, banner and branding are refused by `klub_settings_update` on purpose: the slug would break shared links, the currency locks at the first sale.\n- There is no write path for space ordering, and `groupId: \"null\"` is refused, so a space cannot be sent back to the root. To put a space first, rename the default space, which sits at position 0.\n- Attaching a course to a tier is interface-only: `accessType: ''tier''` is rejected and no `tiers` parameter exists on `course_create` / `course_update`.\n- `klub` returns `counts.posts: -1` by design — that total is not kept.\n\n## Money\n\nAmounts are integers in cents, the currency travels beside them. `analytics_revenue` returns `mrrCents: null`, never zero, when Stripe is not connected: zero would read as \"no subscribers\" when the truth is \"unknown\". Nothing is charged at all until Stripe is connected to the Klub.\n\n## Cost\n\nThe `analytics_*` tools recompute recurring revenue against Stripe. Call them hourly or daily, never inside a loop. Lists paginate with `limit` and `cursor`; `hasMore` says whether to ask again.\n","name":"klubizz-usage","description":"How to run a Klubizz community with the klubizz tools"}],"summary":"Run your Klubizz community: publish posts, manage members and offers, schedule events and read revenue.","category":"marketing","authMethods":[{"id":"oauth","kind":"oauth","label":"Sign in with Klubizz","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://api.klubizz.com/mcp","args":[],"name":"klubizz","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":true},{"id":"key","kind":"key","label":"API key","inputs":[{"key":"KLUBIZZ_API_KEY","help":"Klub settings → Apps → API → create a key. It is shown once. The key carries the Klub and the rights of whoever created it.","type":"password","label":"Klubizz API key","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"klb_live_…"}],"envKeys":[],"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://api.klubizz.com/mcp/${input.KLUBIZZ_API_KEY}","args":[],"name":"klubizz","headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":false}],"description":"Klubizz is a community platform for creators: spaces, posts, courses, events, members and paid offers. Connects Klubizz''s hosted MCP server, which mirrors their public API with the exact same permissions. Requires a Pro plan or above on the Klub."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.03567505,0.03945923,-0.003944397,-0.0029087