('lumail', 'Lumail', 'marketing', 'Manage newsletters, subscribers, campaigns and email workflows on Lumail.', '/services/lumail.png', '{"name":"Lumail","slug":"lumail","inputs":[],"skills":[{"body":"# Lumail\n\nEmail marketing on Lumail. Subscribers: list_subscribers, get_subscriber, add_subscriber, get_subscribers_by_tag, unsubscribe. Tags: list_tags, get_or_create_tags, bulk_add_tags. Campaigns: create_campaign (always DRAFT), update_campaign, update_campaign_with_tiptap, get_campaign_analytics, get_deliverability_score. Workflows: create_workflow, configure_workflow_draft, publish_workflow. Analytics: get_org_stats, get_subscriber_growth. Transactional: send_email.\n\nBefore writing campaign content, call get_skill(''tiptap'') to learn the expected document structure, and get_available_variables for template variables and snippets.\n\nA campaign is created as a draft: never send or schedule one without an explicit instruction naming the campaign. Publishing a workflow or changing its status is irreversible for recipients, so confirm first.\n\nWhen connected via Lumail sign-in instead of an API token, the send, schedule, publish, delete and unsubscribe tools are absent by design: create drafts and hand them over.","name":"lumail-usage","description":"How to use Lumail tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Manage newsletters, subscribers, campaigns and email workflows on Lumail.","category":"marketing","mcpServers":[],"authMethods":[{"id":"token","kind":"key","label":"API token","inputs":[{"key":"LUMAIL_API_TOKEN","help":"Create it in Lumail → Settings → API Tokens → Generate Token. Shown only once.","type":"password","label":"Lumail API token","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"lum_…"}],"envKeys":[],"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://lumail.io/api/mcp/sse","args":[],"name":"lumail","headers":{"Authorization":"Bearer ${input.LUMAIL_API_TOKEN}"},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":true},{"id":"oauth","kind":"oauth","label":"Sign in with Lumail","inputs":[],