('make', 'Make', 'productivity', 'Run Make scenarios and manage your automations through Make''s hosted MCP server.', '/services/make.svg?tone=dark', '{"name":"Make","slug":"make","inputs":[{"key":"MAKE_ZONE","help":"The host shown in your Make dashboard address bar, e.g. eu1.make.com, eu2.make.com or us1.make.com. A token is bound to one zone.","type":"text","label":"Make zone (host)","secret":false,"required":true,"placeholder":"eu2.make.com"},{"key":"MAKE_MCP_TOKEN","help":"Generate it in Make, profile icon, Profile, MCP token. Shown only once.","type":"password","label":"Make MCP token","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"your MCP token"}],"skills":[{"body":"# Make\n\nUse the Make tools to list the user''s scenarios and run them on demand. Each scenario you can trigger is exposed as its own tool; inspect the available tools first, then call the one matching the automation the user asks for, passing any required input fields. Report back the scenario''s output or execution status. Do not assume a scenario exists, only act on the tools that are actually exposed.","name":"make-usage","description":"How to use Make automation tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Run Make scenarios and manage your automations through Make''s hosted MCP server.","category":"productivity","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://${input.MAKE_ZONE}/mcp/stateless","args":[],"name":"make","headers":{"Authorization":"Bearer ${input.MAKE_MCP_TOKEN}"},"transport":"http"}],"description":"Connects Make''s hosted Cloud MCP server so the agent can list and run your scenarios, trigger automations and read their results. Uses an MCP token generated in your Make profile, scoped to your organization''s zone."}'::jsonb, true, true, '[0.026824951,0.013122559,0.03753662,-0.011726379,-0.016159058,-0.045013428,0.025344849,0.065979004,-0.014976501,0.009185791,0.0016050339,0.023880005,-0.02279663,-0.034057617,0.01979065,0.03567505,-0.057006836,-0.0035095215,0.0069770813,-0.003112793,0.018508911,0.005607