('microsoft-teams', 'Microsoft Teams', 'productivity', 'Read and post in Teams channels and chats, search messages and pull meeting transcripts.', '/services/microsoft-teams.png', '{"name":"Microsoft Teams","slug":"microsoft-teams","skills":[{"body":"# Microsoft Teams\n\nTeams are listed by MICROSOFT_TEAMS_TEAMS_LIST and their channels by MICROSOFT_TEAMS_TEAMS_LIST_CHANNELS; every channel call needs both the team id and the channel id. Read a channel with MICROSOFT_TEAMS_TEAMS_LIST_CHANNEL_MESSAGES, open one post with MICROSOFT_TEAMS_GET_CHANNEL_MESSAGE and its thread with MICROSOFT_TEAMS_LIST_MESSAGE_REPLIES. Start a new thread with MICROSOFT_TEAMS_TEAMS_POST_CHANNEL_MESSAGE, answer inside one with MICROSOFT_TEAMS_POST_MESSAGE_REPLY.\n\nChats (one-on-one and group) are separate from channels. MICROSOFT_TEAMS_CHATS_GET_ALL_CHATS lists them, MICROSOFT_TEAMS_LIST_USER_CHAT_MESSAGES reads one, MICROSOFT_TEAMS_GET_CHAT_MESSAGE opens a single message. MICROSOFT_TEAMS_TEAMS_CREATE_CHAT returns the existing one-on-one chat when there already is one, then MICROSOFT_TEAMS_TEAMS_POST_CHAT_MESSAGE writes in it.\n\nTo find something without knowing where it was said, MICROSOFT_TEAMS_SEARCH_MESSAGES takes KQL (`from:alice sent>=2026-09-01 budget`) across every chat and channel the account can see. Resolve a colleague''s name to an id with MICROSOFT_TEAMS_LIST_PEOPLE, MICROSOFT_TEAMS_LIST_TEAM_MEMBERS or MICROSOFT_TEAMS_LIST_USER_CHAT_MEMBERS.\n\nMeetings: MICROSOFT_TEAMS_CREATE_MEETING creates a standalone Teams meeting link (put it on a calendar with Outlook if the user wants an invite). MICROSOFT_TEAMS_LIST_ONLINE_MEETINGS only looks a meeting up by its join URL, it does not search. With the meeting id, MICROSOFT_TEAMS_LIST_MEETING_TRANSCRIPTS and MICROSOFT_TEAMS_GET_MEETING_TRANSCRIPT_CONTENT return what was said, which is the input for a summary or follow-up.\n\nMessages are posted as the signed-in user, in front of colleagues. Confirm the channel or chat and the wording before posting anything the user did not dictate. A 403 on channel messages or transcripts means the tenant admin has not approved the app yet.","name":"microsoft-teams-usage","description":"How to use Microsoft Teams tools"}],"summary":"Read and post in Teams channels and chats, search messages and pull meeting transcripts.","category":"productivity","authMethods":[{"id":"composio","kind":"composio","label":"Connect with Microsoft","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"composio":{"toolkit":"microsoft_teams","allowedTools":["MICROSOFT_TEAMS_TEAMS_LIST","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_TEAMS_LIST_CHANNELS","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_GET_CHANNEL","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_TEAMS_LIST_CHANNEL_MESSAGES","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_GET_CHANNEL_MESSAGE","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_LIST_MESSAGE_REPLIES","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_TEAMS_POST_CHANNEL_MESSAGE","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_POST_MESSAGE_REPLY","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_CHATS_GET_ALL_CHATS","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_GET_CHAT","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_LIST_USER_CHAT_MESSAGES","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_GET_CHAT_MESSAGE","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_TEAMS_CREATE_CHAT","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_TEAMS_POST_CHAT_MESSAGE","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_SEARCH_MESSAGES","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_LIST_TEAM_MEMBERS","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_LIST_USER_CHAT_MEMBERS","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_CREATE_MEETING","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_LIST_ONLINE_MEETINGS","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_GET_ONLINE_MEETING","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_LIST_MEETING_TRANSCRIPTS","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_GET_MEETING_TRANSCRIPT_CONTENT","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_LIST_PEOPLE","MICROSOFT_TEAMS_GET_MY_PROFILE"],"authConfigId":""},"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"${LUMVIKA_HUB_BASE_URL}/api/mcp/composio/microsoft-teams","args":[],"name":"microsoft-teams","headers":{"x-lumvika-key":"${LUMVIKA_API_KEY}","x-lumvika-agent":"${agent.id}"},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":true}],"description":"Microsoft Teams in one click: sign in with Microsoft and your agent can follow channels and chats, post and reply, search conversations, schedule Teams meetings and read their transcripts. The connection is brokered by Composio, so there is no Azure app registration and no token to paste. Reading channel 