('monday', 'monday.com', 'productivity', 'Search boards and create, update, and manage items, columns, owners, timelines, and updates in your monday.com workspace.', '/services/monday.png', '{"name":"monday.com","slug":"monday","skills":[{"body":"# monday.com\n\nUse the monday_* tools to operate on a monday.com workspace via the official MCP server.\n\n## Auth\nConnect either by signing in with OAuth (install the monday MCP app from the marketplace first) or with a personal API token. Find a token in monday.com under your avatar (bottom-left) > Developers > My access tokens. The MCP respects your account permissions, so you can only read or modify data you are authorized to access.\n\n## Typical workflow\n1. Search for the relevant board (by name) to get its board id.\n2. List columns/items on that board to understand its structure.\n3. Create or update items, set column values (status, timeline, people/owner), and post updates.\n\n## Tips\n- Always resolve the correct board id before creating or updating items.\n- Column values are keyed by column id; inspect the board''s columns first.\n- Prefer updating existing items over creating duplicates when an item already matches.","name":"monday-usage","description":"How to use the monday_* tools to work with monday.com boards and items."}],"summary":"Search boards and create, update, and manage items, columns, owners, timelines, and updates in your monday.com workspace.","category":"productivity","authMethods":[{"id":"oauth","kind":"oauth","label":"Sign in with monday.com","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.monday.com/mcp","args":[],"name":"monday","oauth":{},"headers":{"Api-Version":"2025-07"},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":true},{"id":"api-token","kind":"stdio","label":"API token","inputs":[{"key":"MONDAY_TOKEN","help":"In monday.com: click your avatar (bottom-left) > Developers > My access tokens, then copy your personal access token.","type":"password","label":"monday.com API tok