('neon', 'Neon', 'dev', 'Manage Neon serverless Postgres databases, branches, and SQL directly from your agent.', '/services/neon.svg', '{"name":"Neon","slug":"neon","skills":[{"body":"# Neon\n\nNeon is serverless Postgres with branching. Use the Neon MCP tools to:\n\n- List, create, and delete Neon projects\n- Create and manage database branches (great for isolated dev/test copies)\n- Inspect databases, schemas, and tables\n- Run SQL queries and migrations against a project or branch\n\n## Tips\n\n- Create a branch before running risky migrations, then merge or discard it.\n- Reference projects and branches by their IDs returned from the list tools.\n- Authentication is via browser OAuth by default (no key needed), or a Neon API key.","name":"neon-usage","description":"How to use Neon MCP tools"}],"summary":"Manage Neon serverless Postgres databases, branches, and SQL directly from your agent.","category":"dev","authMethods":[{"id":"oauth","kind":"oauth","label":"Sign in with Neon","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.neon.tech/mcp","args":[],"name":"neon","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":true},{"id":"api-key","kind":"stdio","label":"API key","inputs":[{"key":"NEON_API_KEY","help":"Create an API key in the Neon Console → Account settings → API keys.","type":"password","label":"Neon API key","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"napi_…"}],"envKeys":[],"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"args":["-y","@neondatabase/mcp-server-neon","start","${input.NEON_API_KEY}"],"name":"neon","command":"npx","headers":{},"transport":"stdio"}],"recommended":false}],"description":"Neon is a serverless Postgres platform with database branching. Its MCP lets agents create and manage projects, branches, and databases, and run SQL against them. Sign in with browser OAuth, or use a Neon API key with the local stdio server.","multiInstance":true}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.035614014,0.028564453,0.0725708,-0.0390625,0.025756836,0.007972717