('newrelic', 'New Relic', 'dev', 'Query your New Relic observability data (APM, logs, metrics, traces, alerts, dashboards) in natural language via the official hosted MCP server.', '/services/newrelic.svg', '{"name":"New Relic","slug":"newrelic","skills":[{"body":"# New Relic MCP\n\nThe New Relic MCP server connects to your New Relic account so you can inspect observability data with natural language.\n\n## Auth\nConnect via OAuth (browser sign-in) or with a User API key (Api-Key header). US accounts use `https://mcp.newrelic.com/mcp/`; EU accounts use `https://mcp.eu.newrelic.com/mcp/`.\n\n## What you can do\n- Query APM data, distributed traces, logs, and metrics\n- Inspect alerts, incidents, and entity health\n- Read dashboards and run NRQL-style questions in natural language\n\n## Tips\n- Ask about a specific service or entity by name to scope results.\n- Use it to triage incidents: start from an alert, drill into related traces and logs.","name":"newrelic-usage","description":"How to use the New Relic MCP tools"}],"summary":"Query your New Relic observability data (APM, logs, metrics, traces, alerts, dashboards) in natural language via the official hosted MCP server.","category":"dev","authMethods":[{"id":"oauth","kind":"oauth","label":"Sign in with New Relic","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.newrelic.com/mcp/","args":[],"name":"newrelic","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":true},{"id":"api-key","kind":"key","label":"User API key","inputs":[{"key":"NEWRELIC_API_KEY","help":"Create a User API key in New Relic → API keys (one-time UI). It starts with NRAK-.","type":"password","label":"New Relic User API key","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"NRAK-…"}],"envKeys":[],"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.newrelic.com/mcp/","args":[],"name":"newrelic","headers":{"Api-Key":"${input.NEWRELIC_API_KEY}"},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":false}],"description":"New Relic is an observability platfor