('nuxt', 'Nuxt', 'dev', 'Official Nuxt MCP server for querying Nuxt documentation, blog posts, and deployment guides.', '/services/nuxt.svg', '{"name":"Nuxt","slug":"nuxt","inputs":[],"skills":[{"body":"# Nuxt MCP\n\nThe Nuxt MCP server (https://nuxt.com/mcp) exposes the official Nuxt documentation, blog, and deployment guides. No authentication is required.\n\n## Typical tools\n- `list_documentation_pages` - list all available Nuxt documentation pages.\n- `get_documentation_page` - retrieve a documentation page by path, with optional version filtering (3.x, 4.x, or all).\n- `list_blog_posts` / blog retrieval - browse Nuxt blog articles.\n- Deployment provider resources.\n\n## Usage tips\n- Use `list_documentation_pages` first to discover valid paths, then `get_documentation_page` to read content.\n- Specify the Nuxt version (e.g. 4.x) when a question is version-specific to avoid outdated guidance.\n- Great for answering framework questions, generating config, and following official deployment instructions.","name":"nuxt-usage","description":"How to use the Nuxt documentation MCP tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Official Nuxt MCP server for querying Nuxt documentation, blog posts, and deployment guides.","category":"dev","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://nuxt.com/mcp","args":[],"name":"nuxt","headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"description":"Nuxt is a Vue-based framework for building web applications. This official hosted MCP server lets AI assistants browse and retrieve Nuxt documentation pages, blog posts, and deployment provider guides. It is public and requires no authentication."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.03717041,-0.015205383,0.05126953,-0.034729004,0.011550903,-0.028030396,-0.01007843,0.036895752,0.02078247,-0.0028419495,0.025436401,-0.010772705,-0.02519226,-0.020401001,-0.0056533813,0.056671143,-0.059509277,-0.02444458,0.006122589,0.029907227,0.04550171,0.03527832,0.014015198,0.011436462,-0.006385803,-0.012527466,-0.055511475,0.034118652,0.01184082,0.01