('omni', 'Omni', 'analytics', 'Query your governed data in Omni using natural language.', '/services/omni.png', '{"name":"Omni","slug":"omni","inputs":[{"key":"OMNI_INSTANCE_URL","help":"Your Omni subdomain, taken from your Omni URL (e.g. acme.omniapp.co).","type":"text","label":"Omni instance URL","secret":false,"required":true,"placeholder":"acme.omniapp.co"},{"key":"OMNI_API_KEY","help":"Settings → API access → Organization keys → Generate new key. The key is shown only once. Requires Organization Admin.","type":"password","label":"Omni API key","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"…"},{"key":"OMNI_MODEL_ID","help":"Optional. Scope queries to one model. Find it in the model URL: /models/<id>/ide/model. Leave blank to let Omni pick.","type":"text","label":"Model ID (optional)","secret":false,"required":false,"placeholder":"9d9440e5-8522-4507-b092-1ac26ba26673"}],"skills":[{"body":"# Omni\n\nUse the Omni MCP tools to answer data questions against the user''s governed Omni models.\n\n- Query data in natural language; results respect the access controls and business logic defined in the Omni semantic model.\n- Use searchOmniDocs for product or \"how do I…\" questions about Omni itself.\n- If a model isn''t scoped, pick the relevant Omni model before querying. Prefer topics/views defined in the model rather than inventing fields.\n- Present figures with the dimensions and filters used, so results stay auditable.","name":"omni-usage","description":"How to use Omni tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Query your governed data in Omni using natural language.","category":"analytics","mcpServers":[{"env":{"MCP_API_KEY":"${input.OMNI_API_KEY}","MCP_MODEL_ID":"${input.OMNI_MODEL_ID}","MCP_SERVER_URL":"${input.OMNI_INSTANCE_URL}"},"url":"","args":["-y","@omni-co/mcp"],"name":"omni","command":"npx","headers":{},"transport":"stdio"}],"description":"Connects Omni''s MCP server so the agent can ask questions about your data, run governed queries against your semantic model, a