('paddle', 'Paddle', 'payments', 'Manage your Paddle product catalog, billing, subscriptions, and reports through the hosted Paddle MCP server.', '/services/paddle.svg', '{"name":"Paddle","slug":"paddle","inputs":[{"key":"PADDLE_API_KEY","help":"Create one in Paddle > Developer tools > Authentication (vendors.paddle.com/authentication-v2 for live, sandbox-vendors.paddle.com/authentication-v2 for sandbox).","type":"password","label":"Paddle API key","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"pdl_live_..."}],"skills":[{"body":"# Paddle\n\nThe Paddle MCP server connects to `https://mcp.paddle.com/mcp` and exposes a codemode interface with three tools:\n\n- `search` — look up Paddle API methods by name or description.\n- `execute` — run a JavaScript async function that chains one or more Paddle API calls in a single invocation.\n- `report_missing_tool` — flag a missing capability.\n\n## Typical workflow\n1. Use `search` to find the right Paddle API operations (e.g. list products, create price, fetch subscriptions, run reports).\n2. Use `execute` to call and chain them.\n\n## Auth\nRequests authenticate with a Paddle API key sent as `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. The host serves one environment per key — a live key targets live data, a sandbox key targets sandbox. Create keys in Paddle > Developer tools > Authentication.","name":"paddle-usage","description":"How to use the Paddle MCP tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Manage your Paddle product catalog, billing, subscriptions, and reports through the hosted Paddle MCP server.","category":"payments","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.paddle.com/mcp","args":[],"name":"paddle","headers":{"Authorization":"Bearer ${input.PADDLE_API_KEY}"},"transport":"http"}],"description":"Paddle is a merchant-of-record billing platform for software companies, handling payments, subscriptions, and sales tax. This connector uses Paddle''s remote hosted MCP server to let agents search the Paddle API, execute chained API calls, and mana