('pagerduty', 'PagerDuty', 'dev', 'Manage PagerDuty incidents, on-call schedules, services, and escalations from your AI assistant.', '/services/pagerduty.svg', '{"name":"PagerDuty","slug":"pagerduty","skills":[{"body":"# PagerDuty\n\nThe PagerDuty MCP server exposes tools to interact with your PagerDuty account: incidents, services, on-call schedules, escalation policies, teams, event orchestrations, and status pages.\n\n## Auth\n\nConnect either by signing in with PagerDuty in the browser (OAuth) or by pasting a PagerDuty API token — no key is required for the OAuth path. By default the server is read-only; write actions (acknowledging, resolving, creating incidents) require the account to have write tools enabled.\n\n## Common tasks\n\n- List and inspect open incidents; filter by service, urgency, or status.\n- Acknowledge or resolve an incident.\n- Look up who is currently on call for a service or escalation policy.\n- Review services, teams, and escalation policies.\n- Inspect on-call schedules and upcoming rotations.\n\nStart broad (list incidents / services), then drill into a specific id for details before taking any write action.","name":"pagerduty-usage","description":"How to use the PagerDuty MCP tools"}],"summary":"Manage PagerDuty incidents, on-call schedules, services, and escalations from your AI assistant.","category":"dev","authMethods":[{"id":"oauth","kind":"oauth","label":"Sign in with PagerDuty","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.pagerduty.com/mcp","args":[],"name":"pagerduty","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":true},{"id":"api-token","kind":"key","label":"PagerDuty API token","inputs":[{"key":"PAGERDUTY_API_KEY","help":"Create a REST API token in PagerDuty under Integrations → API Access Keys (account-level) or generate a personal User Token under your user profile.","type":"password","label":"PagerDuty API token","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"u+..."}],"envKeys":[],"mcpServe