('postman', 'Postman', 'dev', 'Manage Postman workspaces, collections, API specs, mocks, and monitors, and run API requests.', '/services/postman.svg', '{"name":"Postman","slug":"postman","skills":[{"body":"# Postman\n\nUse the postman_* tools to manage your Postman resources over the hosted MCP server.\n\n## Auth\nAuthenticate either by signing in through your browser (OAuth) or with a Postman API key sent as `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Generate a key under Settings > Account settings > API keys.\n\n## What you can do\n- List and inspect workspaces, collections, and environments.\n- Create or update collections, requests, and environments.\n- Work with API specifications, mocks, and monitors.\n- Run collections and individual requests.\n\n## Tips\n- Start by listing workspaces to get the workspace/collection IDs you need for subsequent calls.\n- The default `minimal` endpoint exposes core operations; broader tool sets exist for code generation and full API coverage.","name":"postman-usage","description":"How to manage Postman resources through the postman_* tools."}],"summary":"Manage Postman workspaces, collections, API specs, mocks, and monitors, and run API requests.","category":"dev","authMethods":[{"id":"oauth","kind":"oauth","label":"Sign in with Postman","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.postman.com/minimal","args":[],"name":"postman","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":true},{"id":"api-key","kind":"key","label":"Postman API key","inputs":[{"key":"API_KEY","help":"In Postman, click your avatar (top right) > Settings > Account settings > API keys, then Generate API Key.","type":"password","label":"Postman API Key","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"PMAK-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"}],"envKeys":[],"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.postman.com/minimal","args":[],"name":"postman","headers":{"Authorization":"Bearer ${input.API_KEY}"},"transport":"http"}]}],"description":"Connects the host