('prisma', 'Prisma', 'dev', 'Manage Prisma Postgres databases with AI agents through Prisma''s hosted MCP server.', '/services/prisma.svg?tone=dark', '{"name":"Prisma","slug":"prisma","inputs":[],"skills":[{"body":"# Prisma\n\nThe Prisma MCP server manages Prisma Postgres databases in your Prisma Console workspace.\n\n## Auth\nOn first use you sign in to Prisma in the browser and pick the workspace to grant access to. No API key is required.\n\n## What you can do\n- Provision new Prisma Postgres database instances\n- Retrieve and manage connection strings\n- Create and manage backups\n- Perform database recovery operations\n\n## Tips\n- Confirm the target workspace before creating or deleting databases.\n- Ask for the connection string explicitly when you need to wire an app to a provisioned database.","name":"prisma-usage","description":"How to use Prisma MCP tools to manage Prisma Postgres databases"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Manage Prisma Postgres databases with AI agents through Prisma''s hosted MCP server.","category":"dev","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.prisma.io/mcp","args":[],"name":"prisma","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"description":"Prisma''s remote MCP server lets AI tools provision, inspect, and manage Prisma Postgres databases in your Prisma Console workspace. It connects over HTTP and authenticates via a browser sign-in to Prisma, so no API key needs to be pasted. Agents can create databases, manage connection strings, and run backup and recovery operations."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.023376465,0.03857422,0.048217773,-0.018997192,-0.0019989014,-0.028945923,0.015129089,0.07470703,-0.013069153,0.010917664,0.01953125,-0.025222778,0.022338867,-0.015686035,-0.026123047,0.021759033,-0.0803833,-0.020370483,-0.012756348,0.06695557,0.033569336,0.04031372,0.023254395,0.02835083,-0.019515991,0.034820557,-0.058288574,0.011871338,0.007499695,-0.020584106,0.013542175,-0.016616821,-0.07714844,0.018173218,0.030807495,0.0055732727,-0.06140