('ringover', 'Ringover', 'crm', 'Make calls, send SMS and read call data via Ringover.', '/services/ringover.png', '{"name":"Ringover","slug":"ringover","inputs":[{"key":"RINGOVER_API_KEY","help":"Create it in Ringover Dashboard -> Developer -> Create an API key (support.ringover.com).","type":"password","label":"Ringover API key","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"Your Ringover API key"}],"skills":[{"body":"# Ringover\n\nRingover has no MCP server; call its public REST API directly with curl.\n\n- Base URL: `https://public-api.ringover.com/v2`\n- Auth header: `Authorization: $RINGOVER_API_KEY` (the RAW key, NOT `Bearer`).\n\nThe API key is available in the environment as `RINGOVER_API_KEY`.\n\n## Common endpoints\n- `GET /calls` - list and filter call history (CDR).\n- `GET /contacts` - list contacts.\n- `POST /sms` - send an SMS.\n- `POST /callbacks` - trigger a click-to-call / callback.\n- `GET /users` - list team members.\n\nExample:\n```\ncurl -H \"Authorization: $RINGOVER_API_KEY\" https://public-api.ringover.com/v2/calls\n```\n\n## Rules\n- Always confirm the recipient and message with the user before sending an SMS or triggering a call - these have real-world cost and reach real people.\n- Never expose the API key in output.","name":"ringover-usage","description":"How to use the Ringover REST API"}],"envKeys":[{"key":"RINGOVER_API_KEY","fromInput":"RINGOVER_API_KEY"}],"summary":"Make calls, send SMS and read call data via Ringover.","category":"crm","mcpServers":[],"description":"Ringover is a cloud phone system for sales and support teams. Connects to Ringover''s public REST API with your API key so the agent can list calls and contacts, send SMS, and trigger callbacks."}'::jsonb, true, true, '[-0.015930176,0.022766113,0.022537231,-0.0027217865,-0.027053833,-0.023361206,-0.0018339157,0.015174866,0.062194824,-0.03112793,0.020233154,0.0004208088,-0.061676025,0.011161804,0.040039062,0.040985107,-0.037902832,0.026794434,-0.015380859,0.050445557,0.0171