('strapi', 'Strapi', 'dev', 'Connect AI agents to your self-hosted Strapi 5 CMS to read, create, update, publish, and delete content.', '/services/strapi.svg', '{"name":"Strapi","slug":"strapi","inputs":[{"key":"STRAPI_URL","help":"The base URL of your self-hosted Strapi 5.47+ instance (without a trailing slash). The MCP endpoint is served at /mcp on this instance.","type":"text","label":"Strapi instance URL","secret":false,"required":true,"placeholder":"https://your-strapi.example.com"},{"key":"STRAPI_ADMIN_TOKEN","help":"Create an Admin token in your Strapi admin panel under Settings > Administration Panel > API Tokens (Admin), then copy the token value. Its permissions determine which content types and operations the agent can access.","type":"password","label":"Strapi Admin token","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"Bearer admin token value"}],"skills":[{"body":"# Strapi\n\nStrapi''s MCP server runs on your own Strapi 5.47+ instance at `<STRAPI_URL>/mcp` over streamable HTTP, authenticated with a Bearer Admin token.\n\n## Enable the server\nIn `config/server.ts` (or `.js`) set `mcp: { enabled: true }` and restart Strapi.\n\n## Tools\nEach collection type exposes up to 8 tools (list, get, create, update, delete, publish, unpublish, discard_draft); each single type up to 6. The Admin token''s permissions determine which content types, fields, and operations are reachable.\n\n## Tips\n- Use list/get tools to inspect content before mutating.\n- Publish/unpublish control draft-and-publish state.\n- Scope the Admin token narrowly for least privilege.","name":"strapi-usage","description":"How to use the Strapi MCP tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Connect AI agents to your self-hosted Strapi 5 CMS to read, create, update, publish, and delete content.","category":"dev","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"${input.STRAPI_URL}/mcp","args":[],"name":"strapi","headers":{"Authorization":"Bearer ${input.STRAPI_ADMIN_TOKEN}"},"transport":"http"}],"description":"Strapi is an open-source headless CMS. Its native MCP server (GA in Strapi v5.49.0) runs on your own Strapi instance at the /mcp endpoint and exposes CRUD, publish, unpublish, and draft tools for your collection and single types. Access is scoped to the permissions of the Admin token you connect with."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.006389618,0.058654785,0.035308838,-0.0056533813,0.012634277,-0.041931152,-0.033477783,0.01751709,0.011795044,-0.022964478,0.0023441315,-0.016571045,0.009109497,-0.012496948,-0.0071868896,0.014328003,-0.03186035,-0.03543091,0.0017852783,0.045562744,0.034362793,0.022598267,0.034179688,0.016921997,0.00033664703,0.013793945,-0.038238525,0.01499176,-0.05908203,-0.013519287,-0.013206482,-0.01197052,0.0071640015,0.011138916,0.04345703,0.02520752,0.019699097,0.019866943,0.010536194,0.026138306,0.0055732727,0.04309082,-0.025497437,-0.0019245148,-0.008232117,-0.010505676,0.0155181885,0.005710602,0.020584106,0.035491943,-0.0009250641,-0.022872925,-0.005584717,0.048309326,-0.011070251,-0.033721924,-0.029052734,-0.028244019,-0.027389526,0.031829834,-0.010894775,-0.03463745,-0.014076233,0.01625061,-0.03237915,0.017623901,-0.009223938,0.020202637,-0.042938232,-0.015792847,0.012672424,-0.0024814606,-0.00013327599,-0.042266846,-0.033111572,-0.05859375,-0.024215698,0.038513184,0.0040130615,0.015289307,-0.0039405823,-0.02168274,-0.06781006,-0.054260254,-0.00868988,-0.031341553,-0.046173096,-0.016189575,0.015701294,-0.0068130493,-0.03515625,0.00055646896,0.010505676,0.0064735413,0.031036377,-0.031402588,-0.02960205,0.0102005005,0.011016846,0.0770874,0.036956787,-0.024780273,-0.04071045,0.0071029663,0.029769897,-0.0018100739,0.08508301,0.022155762,-0.0075569153,0.0012521744,-0.1071167,-0.015960693,-0.03237915,0.016357422,0.024963379,-0.0055236816,0.03326416,0.04949951,-0.01687622,-0.038513184,0.0052223206,0.051971436,0.013587952,-0.051940918,0.024658203,0.0014572144,-0.015533447,-0.012825012,-0.032165527,-0.024276733,0.01663208,-0.025054932,0.0395813,-0.044067383,0.01007080