('typeform', 'Typeform', 'productivity', 'Build Typeform forms, publish them and read their responses straight from your agent.', '/services/typeform.svg?tone=dark', '{"name":"Typeform","slug":"typeform","skills":[{"body":"# Typeform\n\nUse the typeform_* tools to work inside the user''s Typeform account.\n\nResolve ids before anything else. typeform_list_forms returns each form''s id, title, public state and public URL; typeform_list_workspaces gives the workspace ids used when creating a form. Never guess an id.\n\nCreate a form with typeform_create_form and pass the whole question list in `fields` in one call, each field being { ref, title, type, properties, validations }. A new form stays private, so pass settings { is_public: true } to publish it, then hand the user the URL returned in _links.display.\n\nEdit an existing form with typeform_update_form, which takes JSON Patch operations. Read the form with typeform_get_form first so the paths match its actual structure: rename with /title, publish with /settings/is_public, append a question with { op: \"add\", path: \"/fields/-\", value: { title, type, ref } }.\n\nRead submissions with typeform_list_responses. Narrow a period with since/until, search with query, and page through large forms with pageSize plus the before/after cursors. Each answer names the field it belongs to, so match it against the fields from typeform_get_form.\n\ntypeform_upsert_webhook posts every new submission to a URL. The tag is the webhook name, so reusing a tag updates that webhook instead of adding another one.\n\nTypeform allows two requests per second per account, so avoid tight loops over responses.","name":"typeform-usage","description":"How to use Typeform tools"}],"summary":"Build Typeform forms, publish them and read their responses straight from your agent.","category":"productivity","authMethods":[{"id":"managed","kind":"managed","label":"Connect with Typeform","inputs":[],"envKeys":[],"managed":{"provider":"typeform"},"mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"${LUMVIKA_HUB_BASE_URL}/api/mcp/managed/typeform","args":[],"name":"typeform","headers":{"x-lumvika-key":"${LUMVIKA_API_KEY}","x-lumvika-agent":"${agent.id}"},"transport":"http"}],"recommended":true}],"description":"Managed Typeform: connect with Typeform in one click. Lumvika brokers the OAuth and runs the Typeform API calls for you, so there is no developer console to set up and no token to paste.","multiInstance":true}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.028137207,0.051574707,0.023605347,-0.004989624,0.0007138252,-0.015960693,0.014007568,0.03540039,0.016281128,-0.032684326,-0.008132935,-0.009819031,0.032806396,-0.0021362305,0.0074653625,0.022567749,0.023925781,-0.019424438,-0.009666443,0.037963867,0.0234375,0.011505127,-0.023254395,0.0014286041,-0.034210205,0.0289917,-0.07104492,0.04425049,-0.05432129,-0.007297516,-0.025466919,-0.023910522,-0.0013036728,0.03387451,0.03866577,-0.00086021423,0.045806885,0.0055122375,0.04046631,0.018463135,0.011001587,0.021209717,0.023117065,0.022445679,0.0236969,0.013969421,-0.0098724365,-0.0079193115,-0.008598328,-0.0030136108,-0.017791748,0.003452301,-0.011146545,0.0051231384,-0.027450562,0.025756836,-0.041656494,0.002658844,-0.005630493,0.022247314,-0.012969971,-0.031036377,-0.012367249,0.046173096,-0.04547119,0.0027236938,-0.0519104,0.011291504,-0.00944519,0.056732178,0.023590088,-0.043121338,0.023101807,0.039978027,-0.022415161,0.0024375916,0.0038166046,0.05505371,-0.05065918,0.0020332336,0.0056648254,-0.02368164,-0.08843994,-0.0021591187,0.0011329651,-0.019683838,-0.003955841,-0.028778076,-0.064086914,-0.021484375,-0.019348145,-0.003452301,0.0033607483,0.036895752,0.049591064,-0.005153656,-0.037750244,-0.009208679,-0.04815674,0.04147339,0.11218262,0.017822266,-0.047027588,0.038391113,0.0055389404,0.019592285,0.014533997,-0.009101868,0.014595032,-0.033691406,-0.10083008,-0.032684326,-0.012634277,-0.015327454,0.0026721954,-0.0076789856,0.032165527,-0.0010547638,-0.0104599,-0.054504395,-0.026062012,0.013458252,0