('wispr-flow', 'Wispr Flow', 'productivity', 'Search your Wispr Flow meeting notes, summaries and briefs.', '/services/wispr-flow.png?tone=light', '{"name":"Wispr Flow","slug":"wispr-flow","inputs":[],"skills":[{"body":"# Wispr Flow\n\nWispr Flow exposes your Notetaker meeting notes, summaries and briefs through its MCP server. Access is read-only: you can search and read, never create, edit or delete.\n\n## What you can do\n\n- Search meetings by topic, participant or date range, then read the matching notes.\n- Pull action items and commitments out of a call and turn them into tasks elsewhere.\n- Summarise what was decided across several meetings with the same team or client.\n- Recall context before a follow-up: what was promised in the last 1:1, what is still open.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Dictation history is NOT available here, only Notetaker content.\n- If a search returns nothing, the meeting may predate Cloud Sync or Notetaker being enabled on the account. Say so instead of guessing at content.\n- Quote decisions and commitments from the notes verbatim when they matter; do not paraphrase a commitment into something stronger than what was said.","name":"wispr-flow-usage","description":"How to use Wispr Flow meeting notes"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Search your Wispr Flow meeting notes, summaries and briefs.","category":"productivity","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://api.wisprflow.ai/connect/mcp","args":[],"name":"wispr-flow","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"description":"Connects Wispr Flow''s hosted MCP server. You sign in with Wispr Flow in a popup, there is no key to paste. Access is read-only and covers Notetaker meeting notes, summaries and briefs, not your dictation history. Requires Notetaker and Cloud Sync enabled on your Wispr Flow account."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.008903503,0.040161133,0.03253174,-0.0362854,-0.031982422,-0.06298828,-0.017349243,0.04437256,-0.0037441254,0.013206482,0.00082063675,0.04788208,-0.0010519028,0.007843018,-0.