('workos', 'WorkOS', 'dev', 'Manage your WorkOS account (organizations, users, SSO, directory sync, and more) from any AI agent via the hosted WorkOS Management MCP server.', '/services/workos.png', '{"name":"WorkOS","slug":"workos","inputs":[],"skills":[{"body":"# WorkOS\n\nThe WorkOS Management MCP server lets an agent manage your WorkOS account: organizations, users, SSO connections, Directory Sync (SCIM), AuthKit settings, and audit logs.\n\n## Auth\n\nConnecting opens a browser OAuth flow using your existing WorkOS dashboard login. No API key to paste. The agent inherits the exact roles and permissions of your dashboard account.\n\n## Typical tasks\n\n- List and inspect organizations, users, and their memberships.\n- Create or update organizations and invite users.\n- Configure and review SSO and Directory Sync connections.\n- Review audit log events.\n\nAsk in natural language (e.g. \"list the organizations in my WorkOS account\") and the agent will call the appropriate WorkOS tools.","name":"workos-usage","description":"How to use the WorkOS Management MCP tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Manage your WorkOS account (organizations, users, SSO, directory sync, and more) from any AI agent via the hosted WorkOS Management MCP server.","category":"dev","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://mcp.workos.com/mcp","args":[],"name":"workos","oauth":{},"headers":{},"transport":"http"}],"description":"WorkOS is enterprise-grade authentication and identity infrastructure for developers, covering SSO, Directory Sync (SCIM), AuthKit user management, and audit logs. Its hosted Management MCP server exposes the full WorkOS management surface as agent tools. The agent authenticates through your existing WorkOS dashboard login and inherits exactly your roles and permissions."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.014854431,0.03866577,0.04232788,0.013679504,-0.0053634644,-0.00020849705,-0.013191223,0.0070877075,0.008575439,-0.001405716,0.023040771,-0.021972656,-0.0115356445,-0.030059814,0