('x', 'X (Twitter)', 'marketing', 'Read and search posts, users, and trends on X (formerly Twitter) through X''s official hosted MCP server.', '/services/x.svg?tone=dark', '{"name":"X (Twitter)","slug":"x","inputs":[{"key":"X_BEARER_TOKEN","help":"In the X Developer Portal (developer.x.com), open your Project''s App, go to the ''Keys and tokens'' tab, and copy the ''Bearer Token'' under Authentication Tokens. Grants read-only access.","type":"password","label":"X app-only Bearer token","secret":true,"required":true,"placeholder":"AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA..."}],"skills":[{"body":"# X (Twitter) MCP\n\nConnects to X''s official hosted MCP server at https://api.x.com/mcp using an app-only Bearer token (read-only).\n\n## Auth\n- Header: `Authorization: Bearer <X_BEARER_TOKEN>`.\n- Get the token in the X Developer Portal: your Project''s App -> ''Keys and tokens'' -> ''Bearer Token''.\n\n## What you can do\n- Search recent and full-archive posts.\n- Look up users and posts by id or username.\n- Read trends and bookmarks (where the app-only token permits).\n\n## Notes\n- This connection is read-only. Posting, DMs, and other user-context write actions require X''s OAuth 2.0 (PKCE) user login via the xurl bridge and are not available with an app-only token.\n- Usage is billed per X''s pay-per-use API/MCP credit model.","name":"x-usage","description":"How to use the X (Twitter) MCP tools"}],"envKeys":[],"summary":"Read and search posts, users, and trends on X (formerly Twitter) through X''s official hosted MCP server.","category":"marketing","mcpServers":[{"env":{},"url":"https://api.x.com/mcp","args":[],"name":"x","headers":{"Authorization":"Bearer ${input.X_BEARER_TOKEN}"},"transport":"http"}],"description":"X exposes an official hosted MCP server at https://api.x.com/mcp that surfaces the X API (full-archive and recent search, trends, users, posts, bookmarks) as MCP tools. This entry connects in read-only mode using an app-only Bearer token from the X Developer Portal. Write actions such as posting require X''s OAuth 2.0 user-context flow via the xurl bridge and are not covered by this connection."}'::jsonb, true, false, '[-0.0052375793,0.026519775,0.012969971,0.01928711,0.025604248,-0.017608643,0.0019350052,0.03753662,0.018051147,0.009391785,0.006187439,-0.024246216,-0.030319214,0.029403687,-0.022537231,0.03677368,-0.024627686,0.0011968613,0.00024235249,0.053375244,0.023971558,0.038604736,0.011230469,0.0625,-0.022354126,0.00087594986,-0.08892822,0.03756714,0.013916016,-0.0076828003,-0.0099105835,-0.0206604,-0.019454956,0.03237915,0.03237915,-0.022521973,-0.007534027,0.049041748,0.0423584,0.035491943,-0.0029125214,0.0069236755,-0.017166138,0.01966858,-0.033111572,-0.0003170967,-0.0670166,-0.04083252,0.030548096,0.03277588,-9.483099e-05,-0.022949219,-0.052825928,0.034179688,-0.03817749,-0.036987305,-0.02798462,-0.03527832,-0.009414673,0.022659302,-0.049743652,-0.06628418,-0.0049552917,0.0045433044,0.0022029877,0.010986328,0.014625549,0.015457153,0.0052757263,0.04147339,0.01625061,0.011291504,-0.025131226,-0.0031108856,-0.017547607,-0.043395996,0.0042915344,0.04727173,0.0124053955,-0.03527832,0.026306152,-0.008575439,-0.079589844,-0.018981934,-0.016403198,-0.019317627,-0.0054855347,0.010444641,-0.015274048,0.0368042,-0.02809143,0.022628784,-0.0012559891,-0.016784668,0.04348755,0.029144287,-0.045318604,0.026992798,0.0030384064,0.058441162,-0.01914978,-0.017944336,-0.0158844,-0.026733398,0.051635742,-0.028289795,0.010856628,-0.0054893494,0.036071777,-0.021072388,-0.0769043,-0.035308838,0.01600647,0.008621216,0.015991211,-0.04220581,0.023345947,-0.018829346,-0.010627747,0.010444641,-0.034942627,0.09490967,0.020858765,-0.017044067,0.00023686886,-0.03878784,-0.012237549,-0.031921387,-0.03878784,-0.018325806,0.09307861,-0.036590576,0.019165039,-0.037628174,-0.010810852,-0.019363403,-0.008079529,0.0006952286,-0.041656494,-0.0040626526,0.028549194,-0.02432251,0.01739502,-0.014198303,-0.052734375,-0.024383545,-0.05908203,-0.011497498,-0.00299263,-